 him into the alaskan wilderness prospect for gold joined this his lifelong buddy played walter brennan perhaps the western clich xc3 xa9 character end them all but nevertheless enjoyable here always and one else pointedly they are out for themselves and while stewart displays his patented charm come could never really dislike the guy now could are left with little doubt that his basically self centered self interested character none his gosh golly gee humanism allowed come through rather has earned the end the picture the way described above must confront the lawlessness himself and weigh against the need for order and justice which are blatantly lacking the border town which serves the miners starting point their gold dust trail this town ruled tightly its wicked sheriff gannon played john mcintire one the best bad guy performances ever seen comes with much charm and humor and has such relaxed and interesting rapport with stewart that actually takes awhile recognize that the bad guy that when finally sinks does with double force further establishing type breezy necessarily guarded camaraderie between mcintire and stewart the film plays the notion how close temperament they really are and how far moral distance stewart must walk the end the film won through all the twists and turns the plot takes see those for yourself well the rugged and gorgeous alaskan scenery filmed location mind you not cheap painted stills that the studio made what key here how much this story focuses upon character with great dialogue and character interaction substituting for gunplay much the time although the film has just enough action and adventure prevent from ever being static read talky definitely one the greatest performances seen from stewart showing could play the renegade the man man just convincingly the decent and upright guy next door anything fact his everyman qualities lend greater strength his characterization making him seem less mythic overblown like say eastwood john wayne and more three dimensional personage his relationship with brennan well played understated but nevertheless touching with faint suggestion george and lenny from mice and men altogether different type western certainly have more westerns see but this for now favorite and the yardstick which will necessarily judge all the others deserves much better known and appreciated than
