udy and even judy best friend melonie the problem know nothing victor vargas except that the biggest gigolo the neighborhood know that knows how lick his lips and comb his fro and carry himself for the sake wooing girls into the sack but that all know that nino plays piano and quiet well you could see the awards the family piano know his sister nicki gossip loving girl with invested interest watching know that grandma hard working traditional latina woman who trying raise her kids with conservatively world excess corruption yet where the titular character victor vargas this movie somewhere but only know what the movie tells this far the film biggest flaw victor vargas isn much character but ping pong ball bouncing between scenes with judy and his grandmother but never get know who victor vargas really this important because mentioned the only thing know victor vargas that sexually active teenager with libido the size manhattan total alpha male victor vargas not the kind character sympathize with all why should anyone the end the movie the aftermath the climax are truly led believe that somehow victor vargas has attained any depth and learned the errors his ways how could such two dimensional character have any depth only the director had worried little more about fleshing out his main character instead worrying about getting that perfect hand held shot raising victor vargas brings life the world the latino inner city neighborhood the big screen something that few films have done before the past the film has been complimented for feeling real and won argue with that haven seen this level reality since cbs aired survivor seriously although the movie has some nice shots the city the writer director peter sollett was way too dependent close ups and hand held shots this problem particularly noticed indoor scenes that are claustrophobic was forced perform deep breathing exercises keep from passing out the film continues the shots get tighter and tighter with faces cropped from brow chin the screen you can practically smell victor vargas cheap cologne the overall effect unrealistic contrast the indoor scenes inner city apartments make them look small and cramp which not true been those type apartments used live one they not splendorous but they have high ceilings and they decent living spaces the movie standards you think that these apartments were 5x5 cells brick and mortar chipped paint and cracked walls unfortunately sollett constant use close ups and one particularly bad shot with zoom one scene come off totally amateurish but raising victor vargas only sollett second film and his most well known solid effort filmmaking that will hopefully get better continues make films one review read summarized the movie ethnicity for ethnicity sake and cannot agree more victor vargas were truly great film and story then the characters applicability wouldn matter whether they were latino chinese etc yet you were take this story and stick middle class suburbia with bunch teeny bopper white kids the results wouldn such glowing reviews and see the film flaws more clearly indeed some other aspects the use latinos this film bother while some aspects victor vargas are accurate others have question for example victor nino and vicky all share the same room sleep this set off alarm for because seemed contrary what believe any self respecting latino family wouldn have two older brothers sharing the same room with thirteen year old girl first was unsure perhaps was wrong but after speaking with grandmother knew problem with this was justified considering how conservative the grandmother you think that vicky would have been sleeping her room latino who grew somewhat conservative cuban household raised grandmother while mother was working full time could relate the movie many ways which why critical viewpoints are bittersweet because really wanted love this movie unfortunately lack respect for victor vargas sabotaged feelings for the film maybe because victor vargas reminds those guys who were getting laid while was playing with sega genesis when was seventeen maybe because without any further introspection the film victor vargas merely stereotypical hot blooded latino who just end shouting girls from his car hey bay bee want get into luv mah cheen either way don like him ultimately how can like film about him you excuse going stick hands into bowl grits
