nt from the first first blood rambo was unquestionably criminal even though his responsibility for his crimes was lessened severe provocation and his mental instability rambo bona fide all american hero few years earlier the director george pan cosmatos had made the cassandra crossing biased piece left wing anti american propaganda cosmatos however was nothing not versatile and rambo proves that could also turn his hand biased right wing pro american propaganda the one thing the two films have common that both are laughably bad first blood had its faults but also had its virtues its stance that the anti war movement was partly blame for the problems faced vietnam vets readjusting civilian life was controversial one but least the film was trying make statement about war social attitudes war and the roots violence society rambo contrast has very few virtues except that the action sequences are well enough done please those who like that sort thing essentially sort jingoistic revenge fantasy for those americans who were still sore about the vietnam war rambo fights the war single handed and this time the right side wins take that charlie cong this point doubt the film admirers and there seem plenty more than 000 voters have already given ten stars will have concluded that liberal commie loving pinko far from fact have always despised communism pernicious ideology what dislike about the film not its politics but its lack subtlety and its suggestion that the solution all problems including ideological disputes with all guns blazing and try and kill many people possible makes attempt understand the political complexities south east asia why not everyone the region was pro american for all its anti communism the film the sort moronic sledgehammer propaganda that the communists were very good churning out themselves except that they attributed all the world problems capitalism imperialism revisionism whatever other ism they had taken dislike compared rambo the green berets was masterly piece political analysis
