1 |text watched this series when first came out the 70s was years old and watched best friends house dad didn want watch became weekly ritual every sunday and anyone will tell you for two fourteen year olds watch documentary almost reverential silence must mean that this was something special the broad sweep the events world war makes for difficult subject document the makers broke down into what they considered the most significant key happenings and devoted one episode each some episodes covered long periods such wolf pack which covered nearly all six years the battle the atlantic while the battle stalingrad had one episode itself this documentary could not made today quite simply because most those interviewed are dead the list significant players appearing gives amazing insight into the thinking the time anthony eden the foreign secretary carl donnitz head the boats albert speer pet architect confident and later armament minister for hitler one the later episodes see traudl junge hitler secretary who was with him the bunker and was her that dictated his last will and testament she left the bunker after hitler suicide and escaped through the russian lines these and many others play major role the realism the events portrayed have any criticism the series that the code breakers bletchly park are not included but the revelations their part the war only emerged after the series had been made cannot blame the programme makers the opening titles and music are magnificent and lawrence olivier narration lends natural gravity the script the best documentary series ever made without doubt unmissable
