1 |text when heard this film was directed ang lee made sure see this taiwanese director burst into fame with the wedding banquet and eat drink man woman few years ago and then moved sense and sensibility and the ice storm now turns his attention another american icon the civil war this story takes place missouri union state with southern sympathies these never officially joined the confederate army instead they formed outlaw bands called bushwhackers grew they hair long and sometimes would confiscated union uniforms which they wore over their regular clothing the movie depicts their moral dilemma the high drama the times and their supposedly heroic missions killing storekeepers and farmers who aided the union there are stars this movie unless you consider jewel the singer well cast young confederate widow star tobey macquire cast young german farm boy who derided for his heritage because the germans were supposed union sympathizers this young man excellent actor full fresh faced youth whose performance encompasses his wonder and subtle realizations exposed the horror war jeffrey wright freed slave who travels with the bushwhackers because his loyalty the young man who bought him his freedom gives fine and understated performance some the acting however wooden especially the long conversations they have about morality and their costumes are too new and the southern gentleman theme manners and hat tipping and politeness women comes across bit much especially since they make point murder all the men who they pull from their women arms then burn down the stores and houses while don think that this will down one lee ang great movies did find myself fascinated spite the slow parts and its excessive length 140 minutes was interested what was happening next and felt empathy for each the characters who all came across real and imperfect human beings caught the forces history not much action the usual war movie but yet still recommended especially for civil war buffs
