1 |text this police procedural worse than many others its era and better than quite few obviously following the steps dragnet and naked city but emerges enjoyable programmer the best thing about the unadorned look provides into world now long gone the lower class new york the late early here all its seedy glory from the old school tattoo parlors the cheap hotels the greasy spoons these old police films are like travelogues bygone era and very bittersweet anybody who dislikes the sanitized soulless cityscape today also intriguing the emphasis the nuts and bolts scientific aspect solving the crime this case the murder tattooed woman found abandoned car our main heroes detectives tobin and corrigan the footwork but without the tedious and painstaking efforts the lab boys they get nowhere although the technology not the same league the cops here use the dogged persistence investigator track down their man the way some reviewers have written about this movie you think would have been directed wood and acted extras from his movies what bosh enjoyed john miles the gangly marine turned cop tobin had happy lucky easy going approach the role that welcome change from the usual stone faced histrionics most movie cops the period patricia barry cute and delightful his perky girlfriend who helps solve the crime walter kinsella stuffy and droll the older detective corrigan rather liked the chemistry these two and made for something bit different than the sort robotic dragnet approach the mystery itself not too deep and the final chase and shoot out certainly won rank amongst the classics crime cinema but during brief running time the tattooed stranger more than held interest
