1 |text who knew dowdy queen victoria the plump monarch who was virtual recluse for years after the death her husband prince albert actually led life fraught with drama and intrigue her younger days the young victoria not only chronicles the young queen romance with her husband but also does pretty good job detailing the political machinations surrounding her ascent the throne the act set draws you right away following the death victoria father the duke kent 1820 less than year after victoria birth the duchess kent eventually hooked with former army officer john conroy who offered his services comptroller the widow and her infant queen conroy insisted that victoria raised under the atrocious kensington system rules designed prevent the future queen from having any contact with other children while growing what more victoria was forced sleep her mother bedroom everyday until she became queen the film explains that 1830 parliament passed the regency act which established that victoria mother would become regent and hence guardian the event that victoria acceded the throne while still minor during this time the duchess and conroy tried intimidate the hapless princess and insisted that she sign papers making conroy her private secretary and treasurer strong willed victoria would have none and refused along with conroy and her mother nefarious plans the duchess disliked king william she regarded him philanderer who brought disrespect the monarchy the king felt the duchess disrespected his wife result the duchess attempted limit victoria contact with the king over the top scene which seemed actually have occurred history the king berated the duchess his birthday banquet stating that was his goal survive until victoria reached her 18th birthday that her mother would not become regent king william kept his word and died short time after victoria became eligible accede the throne victoria took revenge her mother for her support conroy whom she blamed for making her childhood miserable they were both banished secluded apartment buckingham palace and for number years victoria had little contact with her mother the young victoria conveys the excitement and pomp and circumstance surrounding victoria coronation queen good part the film deals with victoria relationship with lord melbourne the whig party prime minister who unfortunately depicted the film much younger than actually was the beginning melbourne gains the young queen trust and they become good friends the early years her reign she sees melbourne progressive but later loses respect for him somewhat revealed typical politician hiding his contempt for the masses whom supposed championing reality melbourne was more father figure victoria but the film hints some sexual tension between the prime minister and prince albert though they were romantic rivals the plot thickens when melbourne forced out and the queen must commission sir robert peel the more conservative tory party the new prime minister the film chronicles the events the bedchamber crisis which peel resigned after victoria refused replace some her bedchamber ladies with the wives tory politicians the film leaves out another scandal which involved lady hastings one the duchess ladies waiting who was accused having affair with john conroy and becoming pregnant him because her hatred for conroy victoria contributed the nasty rumors being spread about hastings alleged pregnancy turned out hastings only appeared pregnant xc2 x97what she actually had was abdominal tumor victoria inexperience shows during the bedchamber crisis but the film scenarists ignore some the more unsavory aspects her character evidenced the hastings affair the rest the the young victoria deals with course the romance between the queen and prince albert victoria kept albert waiting the film makes clear since she wanted acclimate herself her duties the new sovereign they spent good deal time corresponding with one another until albert returned england and gave victoria support during the trying times the bedchamber crisis find good number parallels between prince albert and prince philip the current queen husband while philip mainly danish went school germany and had laws who were german background both albert and philip made their business reform etiquette the court there great scene where albert discovers that the servants are still setting table for king george iii even though had been dead for years albert struggle was the same for philip xc2 x97as husbands monarchs they had find something both albert and philip became involved various civic projects and proved that they didn have live continually the shadow their ever popular wives fortunately there excellent scene toward the end the film where albert infuriates victoria with what she perceives his interference her affairs albert doesn want second bedchamber crisis goes over his wife head and arranges compromise involving victoria bedchamber ladies victoria barely talking albert when assassin bullets almost cuts them both down the film albert shot the arm but this never happened the performances the film are uniformly excellent especially the principals emily blunt and rupert friend the young victoria ends rather abruptly and the closing credits lean too much toward hagiography mention victoria depression after albert death but victoria still engaging drama and fascinating history lesson
