1 |text group model caliber san francisco women who have been friends since elementary school are suddenly being threatened and attacked someone sending them bizarre valentine day cards who the killer and why the killer after them rating will often change subsequent viewings film sometimes slightly sometimes slightly down however can remember another film where rating has changed drastically has for valentine the first time watched upon its theatrical release thought was pretty awful gave out the equivalent letter grade watching for second time last night can remember what the heck didn like about can only assume that maybe was really the wrong mood watch maybe just didn get any event loved this time giving out might sound ridiculous saying didn get film like this but there something get valentine almost comedy horror director jamie blanks who was also responsible for 1998 urban legend takes the stereotypical teen horror formula that became popular the late 1990s the wake scream 1996 and pushes most the elements notch making valentine intentionally cheesy campy almost the point absurdity where absurdism positive stylistic term top that gives film imbued with humorous commentary romantic relationships the humor unusual that has the same exaggeratedly campy tone the teen horror aspects most the situations the film and the modus operandi the villain humorous not are tied the valentine day theme many viewers will likely subtract points from the film for its various clich xc3 xa9 rooted but implausible scenarios and plot developments however light the above the film intentionally clich xc3 xa9d implausible and ludicrous blanks attempting and mostly succeeding transcend the typical teen slasher mocking spoofing the conventions the genre while also satirizing eros that the attraction the irony basing horror film valentine day incongruity that cleverly woven throughout the film and that itself the heart the slasher genre making prime fodder for valentine extravagant lampooning scream had similar aim with its horror material but the twist there was that the film was self aware valentine day intentionally not self aware the viewer has rely contextual clues for satire lest some think reading too much into the film worthwhile note that blanks said interviews that didn want just another slasher film after urban legend and producer dylan sellers said wanted something more adult other viewers may dislike the fact that valentine day differs much from its putative source material the novel the same name tom savage the novel characters setting and plot are very different from the film sellers has said while was fine book didn think was the right story for film instead the novel which much dryer and more serious tone was used launching pad motif create variations for horror thriller story centered valentine day while those facts won help purists familiar with the book like the film helpful understand why the film has its divergent plot and attitude probably better look the film independent entity with similar theme blanks direction impeccable visually valentine day has lush look throughout with complex deep colors interesting sets and good staging blanks admirable for keeping his villain and attack scenes not too dark with clearly conveyed action also directs his actors with aplomb catalyzing often slyly humorous performances david boreanaz adam carr involved many the funniest moments while valentine day masterpiece very good horror thriller film that seems strongly prone misconceptions you watch expecting something more tongue cheek you may find yourself appreciating lot more
