1 |text not sure why this little film has been banished into obscurity despite some rather silly goings the sentinel clever and inventive horror film that gives most the highly praised ghost stories today more than run for their money michael winner has admitted many times that not the best director all time and that does shine through number occasions with this film but has said that the film works spite uninspired direction and the fact that winner has somehow managed round simply amazing cast talent more than makes for the plot rich with mystery and begins focusing alison parker and her hunt for flat she finds that she can afford most properties she looks but thinks her luck has changed when she finds fully furnished apartment for affordable price her problems start soon after moving she doesn like her neighbours very much and this problem increases when the property broker tells her that she has just one neighbour elderly blind priest the top floor the cast list truly superb with the relatively unknown cristina raines heading great support cast chris sarandon little wooden his role opposite raines but small parts for the likes john carradine eli wallach ava gardner jeff goldblum and christopher walken name but handful more than make for sarandon lifeless portrayal michael winner does good job with his central location the block flats provides creepy and macabre setting for the story the film little slow start but never boring and michael winner screenplay provides surprise that almost impossible guess from the offset which certainly deserves some praise like many similar slow burning horrors this one doesn for the money shot early but unlike many the ending definite climax winner goes all out shock the viewer and the rumour that used actual human oddities true got say that does very good job overall while this film may pure hokum whichever way you look the sentinel one the better films its type and definitely major highlight for its director
1 |text big fan morgan freeman the shawshank redemption ranks the top all time favorite movies but have admit that have often wondered about his choice roles many his titles were big budget clich xc3 xa9s with heart items less for marks the return freeman role that truly showcases his considerable acting talents freeman plays unnamed formerly big time hollywood actor who hasn worked several years has been offered part unspecified indi picture for which doing some research grocery store poor neighborhood after being stranded there his flaky driver freeman offered ride home checkout girl scarlet paz vega whom has semi befriended before she can take him home however scarlet has big job interview she needs get and freeman agrees tag along exchange for the ride the movie follows scarlet and freeman several locations but the movie really just character piece about the interactions between the two freeman the quintessential disconnected hollywood type who hasn heard target and doesn know his own telephone number even what day the week spouts wisdom from the dalai lama filtered thru his the whole world but stage mentality and repeatedly calls scarlet job interview audition and yet has way with people way affecting them that extends beyond his fame fan humanity studies them asks incessant questions about them and delights their quirks where others would simply annoyed scarlet sees the stubborn proud loner that was sees the man used scarlet for her part displays fierce pride and sharp tongue that serve hide her own insecurities about herself vega plays the role with connection freeman that skates the line between almost daughterly love and physical attraction although she plays beautifully and not all creepy sounds but even she feels her connection freeman grow scarlet has keen eye for the reality their different worlds and cuts thru freeman hollywood bull hit with sharp pragmatism that refuses accept anything but the truth the movie smart funny and well written with dialogue that simple but effective read one imdb review that said the lines were stilted which think misinterpretation realistic human speech there are big soliloquies here deep soul searching moments and the trick think show how people ordinary everyday life can forge connections with one another and think freeman and vega pull off beautifully painting picture bond between two people that glitters like sun the ocean ethereal and elusive long after gone lives your memories tantalizing you with what might have been that was bit flowery but really did like the performances and the movie would definitely recommend
