1 |text watching cliffhanger makes nostalgic for the early 90s time when virtually every new action movie could described die hard cliffhanger die hard mountain and pretty good for what but unlike passenger and under siege which are decent die hard clones their own terms cliffhanger dispenses with the enclosed feeling many action movies and embraces breathtaking landscapes that their immensity threaten overwhelm and trivialize the conflicts the people fighting and dying among the peaks years before other movies like simple plan and fargo dramatized crime and murder snowbound locations cliffhanger director renny harlin recognized the visual impact juxtaposing brutal violence and grim struggles survive against cold and indifferent natural surroundings the opening sequence has already received substantial praise all which deserves its intensity allows forget the artifice the camera and the actors and simply believe that what are seeing actually happening not even harlin shot the falling stuffed animal which powerfully effective but still threatens become too much joke and which repeated deep blue sea the ridiculous expression ralph waite face can dim the sequence power the next impressive set piece the gunfight and heist aboard the jet written stallone and michael france and directed harlin the audience plunged into the action not initially knowing which agents are involved the theft and which are not the bloody double crosses are completely unexpected roger ebert has observed the stuntman who made the mid air transfer between the planes deserves some special recognition later during the avalanche sequence one the terrorists thieves appears actually falling the wall snow carries him down the mountain far know one was killed the making this movie small miracle considering the extreme nature some the stunts obviously dummy was used for the shot but the shot itself remains impressive because left wondering how harlin more likely one the second unit directors knew exactly where place the camera take sly stallone action hero any day the week because one the few movie stars ever seen who completely convincing someone who can withstand lot physical and emotional pain and the same time actually feels that pain the role gabe walker really complements stallone acting strengths plays older more vulnerable kind action hero giving impressively low key performance mountain rescuer who must redeem himself contrast many today post matrix comic book inspired action heroes stallone walker ordinary man who becomes hero without any paranormal computer enhanced abilities cliffhanger the hero almost freezes death and his clothes start show big tears barely escapes one dangerous situation after another winces when hit and bleeds when cut particularly the cavern sequence when takes rocky style pummeling from one the mad dog villains should noted that the utterly despicable villains really contribute the movie effectiveness when first saw this movie teenager was rooting for the good guys every step the way and anticipating when another bad guy would bite the dust rather the ice one point actually cheered one the most cold blooded characters the movie deservedly suffered violent demise lithgow british accent unconvincing the movie occasional model plane model helicopter but fundamentally good actor and one the few who can perfectly recite silly dialogue one scene looking his hostages stallone and rooker trying decide which tasks give them actually says you stay you fetch even better actor such anthony hopkins might have had trouble with that line even cliffhanger occasionally tosses credibility aside does only for the sake more entertaining show early the movie for example lithgow openly says one his men retire stallone when comes down real criminal mastermind would have made this mistake even unconsciously his carelessness allows rooker shout warning sly the rock face and this precipitates gripping tug war between stallone and the bad guys trying pull hi