-1 |text heard and read many praising things about midnight meat train which based short story written less than clive barker and supposedly the best adaptation his work since the original hellraiser that directed himself but far can only express very mixed sentiments about viewing experience the most appropriate term summarize the whole film just word nauseating the violence sadistic and extreme which undoubtedly attracts fanatic young horror enthusiasts but also indescribably gratuitous and exploitative normally speaking very pro violence but has least serve some kind purpose the butchering xc2 x96 literally xc2 x96 depicted midnight meat train exclusively meant shock and repulse the viewers with weak nerve systems and easily upset stomachs and even that isn fully effective due the use digital computer effects there are more shortcomings some even bigger than the pointless gore but perhaps should focus the good elements first the basic concept definitely promising and multiple sequences like the chase the freezer room for example are literally oozing with nail biting suspense and macabre atmosphere unfortunately the pacing very uneven and the elaboration the potentially fantastic plot made unnecessarily convoluted presumably the processing short story into long feature film scenario responsible for the pacing irregularities but honestly feel they could have done more with the denouement well with the character played vinnie jones the plot introduces leon aspiring photographer new york whose agent advises search for the truly menacing face the city through sinister pictures leon then becomes obsessed with stalking introvert and suspiciously behaving butcher who always awaits the midnight train leon right the butcher turns out relentless serial killer who literally crushes his victims with big hammer but the killer motivations and behavior suggest there something far more substantial going the rails night midnight meat train takes place naturally unsettling locations like subway stations night and animal abattoirs plus the film also benefices good acting performances and truckload downright disturbing images like cadavers meat hooks and train carriages smeared blood but director xc3 xbbhei kitamura versus godzilla final wars doesn take full advantage all the ending leaves whole lot questions unanswered and even clive barker meant have like this still think deserved slightly more clarifying finale midnight meat train somewhat intriguing and definitely haunting film but not without defaults not intended for easily offended viewers but maybe people looking for plot coherence and clarity should leave alone well
