1 |text love this movie director michael powell once stated that this was his favorite movie and mine well powell and pressburger created seemingly simple superbly crafted story the power love against the powers that however its deception lies the complexity its real imaginary premise basically one could argue that simply depiction the effects war young poetically inclined airman during wwii the question never answered one way the other actually never even asked this continuous understatement part the film appeal the innovative photography and cinematography even includes some nice touches portraying the interests the filmmakers for instance pressburger always wanted cinematic version richard strauss opera der rosenkavalier about young 18th century viennese aristocrat this evident the brief interlude which conductor dressed all his finery holds the rose which appears silver heaven the music even has dreamy quality all the acting first rate david niven his most charming and has excellent support from veteran roger livesey and relative newcomer kim hunter but opinion the film charm comes from marius goring conductor far has the most interesting role filling each his scenes with his innocent lightheartedness brightening the film pity that some conductor scenes were left the cutting room floor also pity that goring comedic talents are rarely seen again film except the wonderful videos the scarlet pimpernel television series from the 1950s this far and away the most memorable role his film career perfect foil for relaxed style niven and his virtual overstatement contrasts nicely with the seriousness the rest the characters ironically also the mid 1940s niven also starred against another heavenly messenger played cary grant the bishop wife their acting styles were similar that found the result boring unenergetic and disappointing note according powell goring desperately wanted the role peter carter initially refusing conductor good thing gave and gave such delightful port