1 |text had initially heard tears kali while back and sounded like something into but with all the films have coming regular basis kinda fell off radar while roaming around the local wonderbook spotted the box for this one and grabbed have say pretty glad did tears kali strange gory sometimes downright creepy film which somewhat constrained obviously low budget but still entertaining and worthwhile watch tears kali centers around the fictional india based taylor erikkson cult group that practices meditation and other rituals the pursuit facing and banishing the individual inner demons but apparently these techniques work either all too well not well enough depending your viewpoint dark forces are not only exorcised but also unleashed upon hapless victims the film told anthology style with short but memorable and eye opening intro sequence and then proceeding into the three stories that make the bulk the film the first shakti about journalist who visits one the cult members who being held mental hospital the journalist goes under cover wanting research the taylor erikkson cult but find that her true motives may hit little closer home when the interview takes violent turn the journalist finds that she may have gotten over her head the second part devi concerns violent young man who sentenced psychological rehab lieu prison sentence for beating young man into coma find that the treating doctor question actually taylor erikkson alumni and his rehabilitation methods are far from the norm the closing story kali revolves around quack faith healer and his assistant who perform miracles for fee when the healer unwittingly helps one his clients and actually expels force which had been possessing her the demon now free roam and looking for new host gotta say really enjoyed tears kali there are some faults with the film that keep from being truly excellent but original and ambitious film for what biggest gripe with the production the poor and uninspired over dubbed dialogue the dubbing sub par and would have much preferred have subtitled option with the original language track some reviewers have said the acting poor which don necessarily agree with think that the dubbing lack luster that makes the performances seem stunted which isn really the case fact few the performances are pretty damn chilling the doctor the second segment and the client the third readily come mind and notable the gore are very well done for low budget film with some graphic scenes eyelid removal via cuticle scissors pencil the throat suicide some decent but irritatingly shaky self flaying and few other goodies thrown for good measure not rough some the more extreme gore films out there but definitely stronger than your average horror fare also found the story concerning the cult group intriguing and welcome change the typical horror story nonsense there are plenty scenes genuine atmosphere and tension the likes which haven come across while although flawed some fundamental ways still think tears kali will appeal most underground horror viewers some scenes may prove too much for the more mainstream viewer definitely recommended
