-1 |text the tragedy the doomed ship titanic has inspired many books and movies the battle between nature and technology always caught man imagination the latest film concerning this tragedy the atlantic ocean was written and directed famous action movie filmmaker james cameron the story titanic involves two fictional characters leonardo dicaprio and kate winslet from different backgrounds one hobo artist the other aristocrat and how their love triumphs over societal barriers and the tragedy sinking ship that they happen first all although using historical name this movie had little regard history the plot was built around two fictional lovers french diamond and treasure hunters the deaths over thousand people the greatest luxury ship its time became mere background many historical facts were simply forgotten where was the radio operator that ignored the iceberg warnings why was there mention the ship that was only miles away from the titanic but did not come the rescue because its captain failed identify the distress signal omitting these facts insult the tragedy and what was the point flavoring this historical disaster with fictional cheesy romance when the story already sad the overall plot was rather shallow rich equals greed and corruption poverty equals compassion and heroism very ironic spend 200 million make movie about how money corrupts there was absolutely human side shown anti heroes seemed like billy zane was playing part the devil casting was also very poor dicaprio was inches shorter than winslet you could swear she was his baby sitter the length the movie was unnecessarily stretched over hours first hour and the half was wasted establishing the relationships between the characters that were known audience long before they went theater and the dialogue that was used made even worse hearing corny pick lines such see you and this side the ship generated more pain than the screams drowning people also jokes were too abundant and rather lame titanic did involve some moving scenes such the part when the musicians were playing while the ship was sinking but they were way near anything original the best thing about this film were its special effects and that the only thing that truly deserved award although this film lacked artistical value overall sense the public could not resist sentimental story starring romeo dicaprio and the movie became success now safe say that the industry will less hesitant invest large amounts money single motion picture seems that titanic did achieve something after all
