1 |text iran women are prohibited from attending live sporting events because the fear that they will corrupted bad language close proximity thousands men and the fact that there are toilet facilities for women the antiquated stadiums based actual incident involving the daughter the director jafar panahi offside follows six girls disguised men who are refused entry into the soccer match 2005 between iran and bahrain match that will decide whether not iran goes the world cup departure from the bleak minimalist films have been accustomed from iran over the last ten years offside exuberant comedy that has patriotic fervor and universal appeal but contains enough subversive social commentary warrant its prohibition from screenings iran shot with digital camera using non professional actors who are more than the task the girls try sneak into azadi stadium tehran but are arrested and placed holding area outside the stadium they are guarded three young army conscripts safdar samandar mohammed kheir abadi and masoud kheymeh kaboud who express ambivalence about their task but are pledged follow the rules the women are soccer enthusiasts not political activists and cheer for iran victory but this does not deter the soldiers from detaining them while they wait for the girls transported the vice squad and uncertain future outspoken rather than acting like victims they continually question the soldiers about the rationale behind the restrictions making their absurdity quite obvious although they can hear the crowd noise the women cannot see the action but achieve minor victory when they persuade one the soldiers provide running commentary the game one the funniest sequences takes place when female prisoner escorted the men room soldier the young recruit then must cope with near riot when has prevent anyone else from using the facilities while the girl still inside little little paraphrase adlai stevenson that which unites them turns out greater than that which divides them and the unlikely antagonists rally behind their country and root for the victory that will send iran the world cup although the point made early and often and the film sags bit the middle offside makes telling point about society where political elite with medieval social mentality has contend with growing group educated and politically astute citizens one can only hope that world pressure and the awakening its own people will force the ayatollahs come terms with the 21st century
