-1 |text the 26th september 1983 short dumpy year old woman stood trial for the attempted murder leonie haddad lady whose husband had recently died and had agreed take lodger who came via housing authority for the elderly haddad was not made aware that her new lodger had fact come fresh from the patton state mental hospital where she had been incarcerated for inexplicable knife attack married couple three years previously haddad soon realised that something was rotten denmark when the woman began lock herself the bathroom with tape recorder reciting prophesies about seven gods haddad fears were confirmed one night when she awoke find her lodger sitting astride her chest holding bread knife announcing that god has inspired kill you haddad managed knock her assailant out with telephone but not before she had lost finger and suffered deep lacerations her face and chest was miracle she survived the lodger was judged innocent reason insanity but sent kicking and screaming back the laughing academy ten years later she was released and found that she was now celebrity but not for the brutal attacks her innocent victims but for her incarnation years earlier when she was known the queen the curve the tennessee tease and miss pin girl the world the notorious bettie page director mary harron mainly known for american psycho takes back the glory days legendary cheesecake and bondage model played solidly enough gretchen mol who inadvertently wrote the blue print for fetish iconography and whose influence can detected everything from comic books catwalks day glo fun ride through evocative depiction the 1950 where page with the familial help good intentioned boyfriends and photographers becomes the number one star pocket sized men glossies with titles like wink tab and parade her real dream movie stardom evades her and brush with the authorities over obscenity charges 1957 the inciting incident which leads her retire from modelling and give herself god the overall style the film light and frothy and only darkens momentarily with allusion her father incestuous attentions and sexual assault which inexplicably appears have discernible effect her mol plays page she seems her photographs happy carefree and fun even the bondage shots betray little more than good humoured incomprehensibility the film ends the upbeat with page cheerfully handing out bibles park with indication the real life unhappy marriages personal tragedy and decent into murderous insanity which lay before her avoiding what think the essential core page story rebirth and resurrection having emerged from decade incarceration page found that her cult had been the ascendance since the mid 1980 and that she had become huge underground icon during which many were asking whatever happened bettie page her mysterious disappearance fed the fires any number conspiracy theories only adding the allure her legend when the world media finally caught with her she gave hint her darker past and she was soon giving interviews for magazines and being photographed playboy parties with the likes pamela anderson and the equally tragic anna nicole smith she found that she was now more famous than she ever was her glory years but the glare this resurrection was only matter time before the full story would come light the only notorious thing about the notorious bettie page they left out the part when she became truly notorious
