1 |text director vincenzo natali first showed his penchant for character based sci flicks with his 1997 short film elevated wherein people remain trapped elevator while unseen monsters roam the building his follow feature project cube released later that year had very similar premise this time with people and instead elevator was vast expansion interlocking cubic deathtraps both were admirable attempts take the sci genre step further deliberately declining show almost any visual stimulation choosing instead spend much time possible focusing the human element how the characters act react and interact under incomprehensible and dangerous conditions after his exploration into the mainstream with 2002 cypher natali has come back his bizarre character film trend bring nothing his latest and far most optimistic and comedic take the wide cinematic world what dave david hewlett and andrew andrew miller are life long friends brought together mutual detachment from society and lack any one else with dave who has always been hindered selfish and somewhat dimwitted nature lives rent free with andrew his ill located and ill constructed house where often takes advantage andrew neurotic and antisocial mentality despite all this the two misfits are happy together until one day their deep character flaws coupled with some astronomically bad luck land them the middle some pretty serious jail sentence worthy trouble top this they discover that their house has been deemed unfit for existence and scheduled demolished before sunset the hazy nightmarish panic everything going wrong for them they wish that the whole world would just disappear and does going any further with the synopsis would compromise lot the film slow occasionally too slow reveal about what happened dave and andrew and how they deal with their new reality natali fascination with studying human behavior under duress ala the birds here spades but simply making the main characters friends rather than strangers able break away from the thriller horror element this premise open more comfortable and optimistic level almost made the aphoristic opposite cube course the film not minutes laughter and sunshine keeping with fundamental realism our two anti heroes dynamic often becomes antagonistic sometimes with rather nasty results like the desert island game the film looks how even best friends when left alone together can fall apart but the same time shows that friends are vital the quality existence very twisted sci way this feel good flick with good heart and good intentions however there are few qualms had with nothing while the two lead actors hewlett and miller well with their parts their characters are not nearly interesting they should have been considering completely them entertain for the better part hour there some development the relationship and personalities dave and andrew some background given but ultimately not enough generous viewer will sit through the less engaging portions the film see through the end but cynics will probably give pretty fast acting mentioned adequate and considering the amount green screen work that would been needed reasonably convincing david hewlett and andrew miller who both wrote wrote the screenplay have been long time friends vincenzo natali hewlett has fact featured every film natali has made perhaps was their creative input that steered this film more positive direction nonetheless the story could have been lot more involving granted relatively entertaining considering that pun intended nothing really happens but you get the impression that more experienced hands lot more could been done with this premise all fairness nothing impressive piece work many ways the concept interesting the direction inventive the script works human level and most all shows progression natali creative mentality for fans his work this will delight and for others will nice way pass little unwanted time just shame that the director fixation human drama prevented from being the great fun film could have been
