1 |text remember being terrified movie blood when was younger and gradually getting less until getting jaded enough sure many other viewers have become that the barrage gory films produced last few years have entertained but not scared made squirm the dentist turned that around the setup seems simple mentally unstable dentist wreaks havoc the insides mouths and perhaps bodies well clever twist though that the dentist the film protagonist instead being some one dimensional bad guy with clear motivation his development the most extensive any character and very human and believable the viewer thus feels sympathy for him well his victims and instead hoping for justice come him found myself hoping would somehow find way cover his tracks and return normal life what really makes horror movie the violence and the dentist does better than any other film can think first off the film has tons tension which something that modern gore films tend lack one scene the dentist emotionally distraught and has see young child patient for the first time reaches into the child mouth you hope that for the dentist and the child sake the encounter ends without injury won spoil what happens second when the gore does come hits all the worst squirmy nerves once again won give anything away course being movie that you never heard does have flaws most importantly exclusively for horror fans also another reviewer mentioned taking place over span just few days don really get any background the characters and the tension drops little bit during the very end but really the fact that would even want know background about the characters evidence how good and the bulk the film solid enough that any small lapses tension can forgiven strange after years being accustomed movie gore suddenly want cover eyes the sight blood the dentist made scared and thoroughly uncomfortable and for this earns full approval
