1 |text remember watching this late night black and white long before live action version was much twinkle peter jackson eye and being very impressed finally getting hands this week vhs copy that was being thrown away and isn that just par for the course had the chance revisit this film and found that still stands quite well although not quite the success that memory had painted have confess certain bias here some reviewers announce themselves confirmed jackson lovers others jackson haters not exactly either was devotee the bbc radio adaptation brian sibley originally broadcast 1981 and instantly recognised the voice gollum here peter woodthorpe would reprise this performance almost note perfect for the radio three years later must say however that where found jackson films increasingly indulgent disappointment the bakshi version for all that has been cut the bone actually more accurate yes there are the usual understandable changes here legolas rather than arwen who substituted for glorfindel the elf sent from rivendell meet the party and there great deal telescoping the action the only exception the latter others have remarked the oddly extended sequence the ford rivendell where the ringwraiths having demonstrated chilling ability freeze and draw back frodo mid flight which they deploy again when defies them after crossing the river then for some unexplained reason simply chase after him prolonged straight gallop which initially nightmarish but pointless plot wise and definitely goes too long would also agree that the balrog unsatisfactory due partly bad animation and that gandalf windmills his arms too much but having watched both approaches the film feel more than ever that the animated route the one take tale that half myth oddly enough one thing that included snippet aragorn story beren and luthien the extreme literalism required live action filming where everything from monsters mail shirts has created detail appear camera counter productive latex faced cgi monsters are less monstrous than sketchily drawn shapes heroic costumes tend look rather silly worn real bodies and hobbits dwarfs with non human body proportions are easy animate but hard film convincingly many reviewers have cited the sniffing ringwraith the woods with its crippled half human movements one the scariest moments the film certainly frightened silly when saw for the first time alone the dark the extreme stylisation the introduction plus voice over done with great skill and economy sum the back story few sentences works very well depict almost mythical era and the change the comic book rusticism the shire particularly like the proudfeet corresponds effectively the similar change tone tolkien prose did feel that there were some missed opportunities where the potential animation could have been used great effect gandalf threatening bilbo with his true power the opening scenes bilbo seeming become gollum like creature under the influence ring lust rivendell and galadriel famous temptation speech all were drawn more less straight where would have been trivial distort the scene reflect the hobbits changed perceptions but generally speaking the changes detail and palette firelight hues bree bright colours emerging rivendell and the fangorn clearing dirty greys and browns for moria and the desolate lands work well reflect the mood the various episodes where live action approach simply doesn allow you blur the background sketch stylised setting fan didn care for either jackson bakshi depiction lothlorien again feel that the radio soundscape was the best evocation come across beautiful slightly uncanny woodland paradise caught out time and feel that bakshi got the elven singing this point pretty badly wrong but like the little montage this point showing the various members the company relaxing together after their travails moria aragorn giving hobbit fencing lesson here charming and equally uncanonical spectacle boromir engaging with the hobbits hollin the jackson version the depiction aragorn convincingly weatherworn ranger good throughout this film viggo mortensen scruffy jesus look really didn work for although would have been interesting see how they planned clean the character the second half for gondor benefit john hurt unsurprisingly gives sterling vocal performance does resonant william squire the part gandalf the hobbits are suspect intended reflect contemporary youth audience identification figures find the animated style their proportions are much more cartoonish than those the human characters works well differentiate them and the whole hairy feet thing drawn here comes across much more plausible than more literal depictions including much fan art personally have less objection boromir viking was always fairly bludgeoning type than beardy aragorn illogical they were both numenorians after all although clearly minority here the big flaw this picture always going the fact that was unfinished project with bizarre tacked voice over ending attempting resolve matters pity would have been interesting not mention less frustrating see what bakshi planned make shelob and minas tirith never mind the dead
