1 |text director douglas sirk once said there very short distance between high art and trash and trash that contains craziness this very quality nearer art this statement defines his cinema perfectly very unique body work that includes classic stage adaptations adventure and war films westerns and course his famous melodramas sirk melodramas were the very word signifies dramas with music the music sets the tone for his masterful style and every stroke his brush sirk was also painter leaves powerful image the screen turned canvas but this ain life but its representation imitation life sirk never tried show reality the contrary none the directors his generation made better use all the technical devices provided hollywood most notably technicolor distinguish the artificial from the real thing let remember that his golden period coincides with the time when hollywood films turned its attention into the social drama blackboard jungle rebel without cause sirk always knew that cinema was meant something else another sirk statements summarizes this you can reach touch the real you just see reflections you try grasp happiness itself your fingers only meet glass defy anybody that has seen written the wind count the amount mirrors and images reflected that appear screen one ends giving therefore are hall full mirrors where there difference between real and its false copy nobody can say that the hadley are real people that town ain real either with those hideous oil pumps all over the place this realm the acting affected the decore fake the trick visible everything pushed little bit off the limit the sexual connotations dorothy malone with the oil tower for example sirk was criticizing and theorizing the same time the angles are the director thoughts the lighting his philosophy written the wind follow the fall traditional way life both geometrical way and terms light and shadows the hadleys house with its different levels connected the spiral staircase operates strictly metaphorical way house that resembles mausoleum that party can cheer tragedy progresses from luminous daylight shadowy night sirk photography becomes extension the inner state his characters and are the colours the clothes they wear drama thus incorporated every element the service the director craft sirk considered himself story bender because bended the standard material was assigned with his style and purpose written the wind good example wouldn work any other hands the other director that was using similar strategies was frank tashlin who was for comedy the same that sirk was for melodrama their films are full the machinery american life advertising sets jukeboxes washing machines sport cars vacuum cleaners depict its emptiness and decay inclined think that their films were regarded different way their contemporary audiences the game was played both sides was camp now regard them cult bizarre because are not those spectators anymore that why todd haynes homage far from heaven turns into pastiche because reproduces sirk work nowadays nothing happened between then sirk turns exactly into that painting hanging the art gallery that julianne moore and the gardener discuss the aforementioned film sirk understood the elements melodrama perfectly there were always immovable characters rock hudson and lauren bacall here against which could assemble series split ones his balance through antithesis remarkable and not surprisingly root for the split characters because these are the ones sirk interested too when robert stack flies the plane and tempts lauren bacall with all sorts mundane comforts the world below them obvious faustian echoes are strangely fascinated with him too are when the devilish nymphomaniac little sister painfully evokes her past with mitch alone the river the sirk universe the studio often imposed happy ends have negative impact fact they worked just great sirk was fond greek tragedy and considered happy endings the deux machinea his day thus the final courtroom scene fits well and one must also remember that the whole film told flashback know from the very beginning that tragedy will fall nevertheless over the hadley feud was pointed out the many similarities between written the wind with the godfather saga absolutely agree and sure the parallel not incidental both share the theme the old powerful father head trying keep his empire going while protecting his family the temperamental son portrayed robert stack has amazing physical resemblance with jimmy caan sonny corleone the action fighting her sister male friend symmetrical the non son which the old man put his trust also common both films the fact that both families carry the names their town even details the gate that gives access the property and the surroundings the house covered leaves suggest that coppola had written the wind mind while setting his masterwork because both films deal with the subject power the acquisition power its manipulation and legacy even kyle hadley sterility the event that hastens the turmoil issue easily tied the central theme power this case weakness sexual power the other great film that deals with power and uses american life its representation citizen kane one wouldn think first similarities between welles and sirk films but there are good many starting with the petrol business the origin the family fortune and ending the fact that mitch wayne rock hudson charles foster kane was adopted tutor having his own father alive amazingly the same actor harry shannon perform both wayne and kane fathers this detail cannot coincidence written the wind masterpiece every aspect execution and vision style and technique highlight the career this wonderful director some say that this his best film opinion magnificent obsession all that heaven allows there always tomorrow and imitation life are just good and for those who put sirk the level dallas dinasty wish them happy end
