1 |text took year old daughter see nancy drew over the weekend and found myself thoroughly entertained first off was clean and mean standards the majority kids movies today are full crude toilet humor and gross out jokes elicit cheap laughter from the pre teen crowd nancy drew smarter than that however and the humor subtle and clever the title role played with refreshing vivaciousness emma roberts who perky and polite without ever becoming annoying unlike the brady bunch movie where the anachronistic characters are jeered and ridiculed nancy style treated with respect and dignity great moment when the style conscious girls with their paris hilton streetwalker attire are dismissed the boutique owner while nancy her penny loafers and homemade butterick pattern dress embraced this movie shuns the need enlighten this wholesome girl tack many hollywood movies take nancy remains true herself and her values throughout the mystery just tense enough times engaging there were several suspenseful moments where daughter nervously grabbed arm but there were gratuitous shock scenes all based tension and mood and lot fun the supporting cast good particularly marshall bell the creepy caretaker there are some great cameos eddie jemison chris kattan and bruce willis and many moments that will make adults smile this film deserves better ratings than some have given not only was glad not dragged yet another computer animated film where talking animals burp and pass gas all over the place but was also very entertained had been there without child still would enjoyed the movie this one dvd that will have daughter name under the christmas tree
