1 |text what the movie the 60s really represents those who growled around the belly america those times the turbulence and diversity the decade despite the exaggerated stereotyped characters the genuineness the issues remains clear not only were those radical times change but also very confusing times two basic things changed our world then the 1964 civil rights act and the overwhelming influence the media those two new freedoms began social changes that soon became institutionalized from chaos came sensitivity from disorder came values bear mind however that the bulk americans were not involved this they worked they played they watched the news and slowly they became effected the efforts and struggles the minorities the civil rights workers the political activists the anti war efforts the war poverty the representation the power the press and particular was well reflected although the conflict between the general public attitude and those seeking change things was best ignored and worst misrepresented middle class americans weren all standing around angrily holding baseball bats disowning their wayward daughters they were confused too let not forget how folk singers suddenly became protest singers and how the beatles began onslaught that killed the folk protest movement there are beatle songs the movie even any mention them think you didn live the decade you might not have sense what the movie about the overall picture bit dim one point held down steady job while sister lived the hog farm commune and went woodstock another point was haight asbury and the detroit riots while she worked and played the housewife maine and connecticut roles were constantly changing the movie depicts three siblings middle class family they represent the hippie child the political activist and the active military personnel dad represents the typical attitudes and mom represents the voice reason tolerance and sometimes compromise for the sake peace the black family comprises minister and his son disproportionately think assume the producers knew all the variables and had settle limitations else the film would have become long boring documentary dad message was that anger produces bitterness and bitterness produces chaos was clearly message directed today youth are looking unique solution social problems and also how issues divide the 60s were unusual that way and only the roaring 20s compare other words this movie has moral after all the end our collective individualism that survives put that your oxymoron list everyone was god guru free spirited genius the 60s was time magic and madness one will ever nail the 60s down right was too diverse this movie close least can say are not ashamed that learned and grew from and that for once generation shaped and changed america for the better
