1 |text moonchild very difficult movie categorise easiest think several snapshots the lives the two central characters the fact that these characters are members street gang set multicultural city the near future and that one them vampire does not preclude them from having moments like any other people and this one the places where this movie different anything else ever heard doesn get wrapped the fact that one the main characters vampire just something that has dealt with like any other problem the way the characters interact surprisingly realistic there are embarrassing relatives and tricks that are meant look cool that just don work which leaves the film with lovely sense not taking itself too seriously for the most part the other area that really stood out the languages the fictional city mallepa contains various cultural groups and characters speak the language that they would expected speak japanese gang members speak japanese each other but chinese when talking characters chinese descent possibly the most amusing exchange involves australian and conducted english the actors the four arguably main characters have three separate mother tongues between them and speak varying levels each others languages quite feat that the movie was made all which suppose brings the lead actors much has been made the fact that the movie stars two japan biggest rockstars gackt and hyde well taiwanese superstar lee hom wang whether praise them for their acting criticise simply fangirl about them opinion lee hom the best playing straight and realistic character however any lack acting ability gackt part mostly masked the fact that the character plays prone being over dramatic wasn sure hyde character was supposed sulky and sarcastic came across but doesn really detract from the movie either way there are several scenes which take rather melodramatic turns which made difficult for them affect much emotionally although this doesn seem stop lot people found best just enjoy the movie for what and not take too seriously perfect for getting out and watching with group friends does have its flaws but overall was very enjoyable and highly recommend anyone who doesn mind few subtitles
