1 |text knew absolutely nothing about chocolat before viewing didn know anything about the story the cast the director anything about the film history all knew was was highly acclaimed french film had known more probably wouldn have viewed the picture with open mind paper the premise doesn sound interesting had known what chocolat was about ahead time interest while watching would have been limited however not knowing about the story helped enjoy throughout had clue has where the story would what the characters would and what the end result would was nothing else not predictable film indeed could have been the story told flashbacks telling story flashbacks often risky move the part the filmmakers since the lead character seen present day the audience knows she will remain alive using the flashback technique director claire denis able ensure the audience that the young girl makes adulthood without any serious physical damage giving the viewer the sense that chocolat story more about emotions than what the outside lesser filmmaker would give france haggard looking face one that screams confused and unusual childhood instead denis presents france beautiful girl someone who looks fine the outside could argued that chocolat more about france mother since she given far more screen time though believe ultimately about france what chocolat really about how mother actions affect her daughter about how parents behavior stays with their offspring france not ruined her mother actions the story yet her mother actions clearly made impression france had france not been affected all her mother actions the flashback aspect would irrelevant for movie that deals with two time periods the past and the present chocolat was very well paced there were scene excess fat none the scenes felt gratuitous out the place the film had nice rhythm the editing crisp leaving only what was necessary tell the story with well told story solid editing and organized directing chocolat one the better french films have seen was responsible for launching claire denis career and with good reason incredible directorial debut
