1 |text there aren many overcoming the odds stories quite like that christy brown born with cerebral palsy 1930s dublin his parents thought his handicap was mental well physical though eventually properly diagnosed brown lower working class family with nearly children had push himself just appreciated his family through the use his only fully functioning limb his left leg taught himself write and paint both skills developed expertly but what makes the film version brown autobiography left foot such great retelling its humility both director writer jim sheridan and star daniel day lewis have managed tell this story way that doesn scream for attention and resort melodrama cheesy struggles and scenes frustration well glorious moments minute victory are easy pitfalls story miraculous yet left foot stays real and intrinsically inspired day lewis the easiest highlight playing anyone with such serious physical impairments has demanding task not only does day lewis give very complete picture christy but also manages chronicle the growth improvement and inner change the character different stages his life plays christy when had limited language capability and was emotionally volatile just crisply does the intellectually learned christy who struggles cope with why can find non platonic love the latter theme the film strongest and would been nice for sheridan and adapter shane connaughton really flesh that out regardless day lewis gets understand and sympathize with all those elements giving performance that believable you often don have time think wow such great actor those are the most commendable performances equally important but through more subtle means sheridan work the film this story about day day life and struggles although christy has such unique set circumstances hampering his life his struggles are not unlike our own and sheridan grasps that concept completely christy struggles with love parental attention questions self worth and capability his struggles are just more physically manifested literally and figuratively than ours sheridan gives moments that capture the spirit the large brown family and christy unique place the drama evolves naturally when tensions are highest and the humor comes much the same way the dinner scene when christy learns that his doctor teacher the woman loves going marry his brother peter the film finest example both day lewis and sheridan efforts built well sheridan that comes out when ready and day lewis takes from there with his stunning work the other strong component the film brenda fricker mrs brown did not know she won the oscar but there was something about her performances christy loving and wise mother that just screamed oscar worthy her love for christy and constant fighting for him just seems convincing and heartfelt and she earns lot sympathy given her situation the emotional punch the film given the story surprisingly minimal perhaps that was part the sacrifice trying create film that feels organically human the two should reconcilable but imagine challenging tell story that feels true life and one that provides enough dramatic moments take our emotions roller coaster the choice downplay the latter was definitely the wise one for left foot brown circumstances speak for themselves they don need squeezed for weightier dramatic impact steven visit site moviemusereviews com for more
