-1 |text around the late 1970 animator don bluth frustrated with the output his company disney was churning defected from the mouse house form his own studio his first production the secret nimh was brilliant feature that still holds well this day this was followed american tail and the land before time both which were made under the involvement steven spielberg and were commercially successful although none those two films had the dark adult appeal nimh they still are very charming enjoyable features for both children and grown ups but before long don bluth had his first major misfire with all dogs heaven critics were especially harsh this film and matters weren helped the fact that opened alongside disney the little mermaid considering that the movie has such friendly sounding title one would expect all dogs heaven pleasant family fare instead bluth provides surprisingly dark story involving gambling deceit crime mistreatment and murder that itself not problem for animated feature per say but does call into question over whether the film for children the other hand hard say whether adults will find much enjoy all dogs heaven short movie with major identity crisis set dreary junkyard new orleans the movie starts out when charlie barkin rough and tumble german shepherd run over car courtesy his former gambling casino partner nasty cigar puffing pitbull carface before you know charlie finds himself heaven albeit default here whippet angel annabelle tells him that all dogs heaven because unlike people dogs are usually loyal and kind this line represents the confused nature the movie since the dogs the movie the whippet aside are presented anything but upon realizing that been murdered charlie steals his way back earth and plots get even with carface with the reluctant help his dachshund pal itchy charlie rescues carface prize annemarie human girl who can talk animals order predict who will win the rat races charlie claims that will help the little cutie find her family but reality using her skills win fortunes the race that can build more elaborate casino his own bring carface down although refuses admit charlie does grow love annemarie the concept the story isn problematic the execution aside from the human girl annemarie and flamboyant musical alligator who appears about three quarters through with the vocal pipes ken page none the other characters emerge likable nor frankly are even worth caring about unfortunately that also applies charlie trying make him anti hero the script composed more than ten writers only succeeds rendering the character too unlovable such the audience feels empathy for charlie and worse his redemption the end the movie does not come across convincing further damaging the character the disappointingly uncharismatic vocal performance from burt reynolds besides the lack endearing lead the movie other problem the structure the story the slowly paced plot jumps all over the place and makes habit throwing extra scenes which serve purpose but pad out the movie running time the aforementioned musical alligator who resides danky sewer infested with native rats seems have been thrown from nowhere does scene where charlie tries show his generosity annemarie feeding pack pastel colored pups pizza the whole screenplay feels like rough first draft bit more polish could have made this tighter impactful story matters are not helped the lackluster musical numbers charlie strouse and kuenster annemarie song and the gator ballad are the only good ones the latter particular benefits from ken page mellifluous vocal the uneven voice cast mentioned burt reynolds stiff and lifeless charlie detracts from his already unlikeable character even further the only exception fiery confession itchy about his true intentions toward the end dom deluise itchy pretty good but had better roles notably tiger american tail and jeremy the secret nimh ken page mentioned awesome anything does but his character has such small part that his overall contribution unremarkable best similarly wasted are loni anderson collie who once sired litter with charlie melba moore and charles nelson reilly judith barsi annemarie probably the only voice that comes across truly memorable partially because her character the sole legitimately likable one this depressing and joyless show barsi aside the only real positive about all dogs heaven the animation technically this film has some the most imaginative visuals from bluth team 1980 standards that particularly frightening scene where charlie has nightmare about ending fiery underworld ruled gargantuan satanic canine demon anything the movie more triumph animation than storytelling the whole however cannot recommend all dogs heaven good entertainment even though recognize that the movie has its fans and the climax does admittingly provide some energy and moving conclusion the overall package not the same league bluth better efforts animation buffs will marvel the lush artistry but the time over all dogs heaven could very well leave bad taste your mouth
