ithout his permission and spliced several shots from molina earlier movies all this pretty much ruined any chance this movie had being one molina best works and surprise that the two them never worked together again but not all bad news there are some good ideas here some aspects the storyline make interesting psychological drama with the werewolf metaphor for jealousy and rage the werewolf yeti idea one that returned molina later work some pretty horrific and surreal stuff goes down the cellar and there also very memorable sequence about half way through the film where daninsky runs from house house through village slaughtering molesting innocents goes one scene particularly intense but actually lifted straight from molina first movie marca del hombre lobo along with few other shots actually found the movie the whole very entertaining although there are some problems with the front row entertainment version such pretty obvious cuts although some may simply due the director lack continuity gods knows what omissions there are probably try get hands the uncut version some stage the future this overall decent piece vintage naschy which experienced fans might enjoy but could have been much better and probably wouldn make great introduction
