een jeffrey and cole the madhouse are the best the movie pitt eyes voice and quirky mannerisms convince you really crazy guy locked warped logic only understands pitt oscar nomination was well deserved surprising was also bruce willis performance his didn remember very well but beautiful and full sensibility plays man who spent almost all his life underground and when comes the past you share his childish fascination with something simple breathing the fresh air the morning watching the sun cole rather ambiguous character peoples tried imbue some darkness him and does other disturbing things other people and himself the scene where removes his own teeth reveals how far his dementia has gone unchecked ironically cole didn start crazy character but when starts warning everyone about the end the world considered mad and convinced all his mind until arrives point when can distinguish past from future reality from fiction willis spends lot time looking confused and insecure and works perfectly one the fun twists the narrative when cole shrink kathryn railly finds undeniable proof really from the future and now has convince him again his mission save the world the screenplay full with weird twists like this and keeps the movie fast pace their relationship also well handed although perhaps bit compressed for time sake but enjoyed watching cole and railly falling love and trying escape the authority the future live peaceful life the past but then things end tragic bittersweet climax airport wrapping all the pieces together which will blow many minds away there are two great endings this movie twist the sense se7en fight club and more intimate ending where railly crouching next cole who just been shot and looking around for younger james cole who witnessing his future self die the two share brief look and she smiles him the twist brilliant but prefer this ending for emotional impact madeleine stowe very good playing railly she drew many different emotions from her performanc