1 |text what brilliant film will admit very ambitious with the subject matter little over two and half hours very long film too but neither these pointers are flaws any way cry freedom despite the minor flaws may have powerful moving and compelling film about the story the black activist steve biko his struggles awaken south africa the horrors the apartheid true that the first half stronger than the second terms emotional impact people have also complained that the film suffers from too much woods not enough biko may wrong but although biko story told the perspective woods woods important character conveying biko story the world cry freedom visually looks amazing with the show stopping cinematography and the stunning south african scenery was visual feast the opening scenes especially were brilliantly shot george fenton music brought real dramatic weight most scenes was subtle scenes the second half but stirring and dramatic the crowd scenes the script was exceptional quality the courtroom scenes with biko were enough really make you think wow this real quality stuff the first half with biko the main focus constantly had something feel emotional about whether was the police attack the south african citizens biko death the second half entirely about donald woods carries less emotional punch but compensated how shot performed and written and there are parts that are genuinely suspenseful well the performances were exceptional from the entire cast from the most minor character the two leads there wasn single bad performance regardless the accents that but forgiven easily how much the performances draw you denzel washington one his more understated performances gives truly compelling performance biko and kevin kline shows that can good drama comedy for gave suitably subtle performance match that washington and the two men chemistry believable and never strikes false note penelope wilton lovely donald wife wendy and she great actress anyway out the supporting performances and there may some bias two stood out for one was timothy west who relishes his role captain dewet the other was the ever exceptional john thaw brilliantly chilling cameo role kruger lord richard attenborough direction focused and constantly sensitive usual overall truly wonderful film ambitious and long but never ceases compelling powerful and achingly moving definite winner from lord richard attenborough and worthy lot more praise bethany cox
