1 |text although grateful this obscure gem italian exploitation cinema features the recently released grindhouse experience box set and although also available disc under the misleading and stupid alternate title escape from death row honestly think deserves proper and luxurious dvd edition completely its originally spoken languages with subtitle options the dubbing truly horrible restored picture quality and truckload special bonus features heck don even need the restored picture quality and bonus features only could watch the film its original language mean frank and crazy tony cheerfully fast paced mafia crime flick with lot violence comedy which admittedly doesn always work feminine beauty and two witty main characters tony bianco terrific the small thug pretending the city biggest don when the real crime lord frankie dio lee van cleef arrives town sees opportunity climb the ladder offering his services frankie initially ignores the little crook but they eventually form unlikely team when frankie entire criminal empire turns against him and new french criminal mastermind even assassinates frankie innocent brother tony helps frankie escape from prison and together they head for marseille extract frankie revenge the script this sadly neglected crime gem funnily alters gritty action suspense with light headed bits comedy like the grotesque car chase through the narrow french mountain roads for example the build towards the typical mafia execution sequences guided excellent riz ortolani score are extremely tense and the actual killings are sadistic and merciless which probably why the film considered somewhat grindhouse classic the film lacks strong female lead the lovely and amazingly voluptuous beauty edwige fenech sadly just appears couple scenes and then still the background the men behind the camera responsible for the superb cinematography was less then joe amato great film highly recommended fans italian exploitation and hope watch again soon its original version
