1 |text generally not huge fan stop motion films and first ruka didn capture attention however knowing that this film was made the repressive czechoslovakia during the soviet domination era the more watched the film the more realized just how subversive this innocent looking little film was this subtext really made the film come life and gives real staying power both work art and political statement the sad little film done without any dialog but pretty clear what happening cute little wooden man making clay pot and having lovely time when suddenly meddling animated hand appears and destroys the pot making into sculpture hand instead well the wooden man tries again and again chase away the hand and his own thing however over time the hand becomes more and more insistent and eventually cages the man and the end the man dead thanks the meddling hand and the hand sign real hypocrisy gives the man hero funeral said this film obvious attempt the brave jir xc3 xad trnka criticize his domineering government not surprisingly though czechs loved the film and gave critical praise the state the hand banned this little parable sadly trnka did not live see his nation liberated little more than two decades later during the called velvet revolution
1 |text 1958 the sleepy small southern town clarksburg evil sheriff roy childress the almighty vic morrow peak nasty form cracks down super hard speeders forcing said offenders off cliff their untimely deaths especially dangerous stretch road childress meets his match when cool young hot rod driver michael mccord splendidly smooth and brooding portrayal martin sheen shows town his souped automobile with the specific intention avenging the death his brother sheen real life sibling joe estevez brief cameo director richard heffron working from taut and intriguing script richard compton the same guy who directed the drive movie gems welcome home soldier boys and macon county line relates the gripping story brisk pace neatly creates flavorsome period setting and ably milks plenty suspense out the tense game wit and wills between childress and mccord the uniformly fine cast helps lot sheen radiates brash james deanesque rebellious vibe the lead morrow makes the most out his meaty bad guy part plus there are excellent supporting performances michelle phillips sweet diner waitress maggie stuart margolin folksy deputy nick nolte amiable gas station attendant buzz stafford gary morgan buzz endearingly gawky younger brother lyle janit baldwin sassy local tart sissy britt leach stingy cab driver johnny and frederic downs the stern judge hooker the climactic vehicular confrontation between childress and mccord real pulse pounding white knuckle thrilling doozy terry meade sharp cinematography the well drawn characters for example childress became obsessed with busting speeders after his wife and kid were killed fatal hit and run incident the groovy syncopated score luchi jesus and the beautiful mountainside scenery all further enhance the overall sound quality this superior made for winner
