1 |text waqt perfect example chicken soup not exactly for your soul the broth unfortunately has lost its actual taste thanks all the excess dilution and garnishing that went into its making what surprising and disappointing about waqt that comes from director who stayed away from the usual clich xc3 xa9s hindi cinema his first venture but who his second outing gives for all the stereotype film formulas while vipul shah had the conviction show something implausible blind men robbing bank aankhen just fails induce life the entire packaging waqt that based something conceivable father son relationship adopted from gujarati play aavjo vhala fari malishu waqt does have sensible storyline with social message back mature look the father son relationship father unconditional love towards his son and son responsibility towards his family ishwar chand sharawat amitabh bachchan who has established his entire empire his own from the scratch leads affluent life with his wife sumitra shefali shah their only son aditya akshay kumar never had the need strive for anything since got everything tailor made and spoon fed life ishwar pampering has only spoil him all the more aditya dreams turning into superstar but does nothing make his dreams come true the meanwhile marries his ladylove mitali priyanka chopra ishwar hopes that marriage will make aditya more responsible man but disappointed aditya still his blithe best leading carefree life the endurance limit finally collapses when ishwar expels aditya from his house the sudden change the attitude his affectionate father towards him and his now expecting wife baffles aditya has option left but strive for the livelihood his wife and his unborn kid starts turning into independent man but the rift the relationship between him and his father grows the story simplistic while the uncomplicated screenplay has very elementary approach one can easily identify and relate with the credible characters both the father and the son you are not one the two you least might have come across individuals like them somewhere real life add director vipul shah easy handling the screenplay with family affair like this any other director his place would have added tons melodrama the proceedings per the cinematic laws bollywood family dramas turning the film into compulsive tearjerker however shah excels the effortless handling emotions for most part the film clear cut example his unpretentious direction palpable the pre interval scene where the father expels the son from his house rather frivolous manner the purpose the scene achieved without blotting brunt the audiences brains ditto for the scene the second half wherein the now separated father son have flippant conversation that what differentiates waqt from kabhi kushi ghum rishtaa and fact places one level high terms treatment but after gaining all the distinction points one may wonder where does waqt still fail the problem lies the fact that while waqt distinguishes itself from the others league terms treatment gives the glitches the terms packaging what with the director forcing song dance every now and then the first half there johar kinda shaadi song chopra kinda holi song father son disco dandia song dream song and dream come true song inducing sufficient yawns the viewer picture this the father has just ousted the son from his house and the son dreaming song moroccan mountains with his wife out place out reason and the audience out seat the film just drags the first half and the actual story starts only the second half the director has wasted too much waqt unnecessary elements the much talked about dog chase sequence isn bad but not redeeming either however akshay kumar taandav dance simply ridiculous imagine qualifies for the star hunt the movie with this unintentionally hilarious histrionic add the climax set the finals the star hunt where the son bursts out with emotions that archetypal also the editing pattern could have been reversed conceal the father reason for the change attitude towards his son anu malik music fine though unnecessary the proceedings santosh thundiiayil camera work competent enough though not much demanding aatish kapadia has come with some good dialogs for dramatic moments boman irani and rajpal yadav make the light moments the film very efficiently while rajpal yadav has been going overboard with his comic histrionics many films off lately this time underplays his character and completely restrained his deadpan expressions are perfectly complimented with boman over the top histrionics shefali shah convincing the mother role not taken censure but she flawless both playing and looking her character priyanka gorgeous and performs her part well course the major applause deserves are akshay kumar and amitabh bachchan akshay especially expressive the scene where his doting father intentionally berates him make him aware his responsibilities though bachchan goes bit dramatic couple scenes his brilliance strikes throughout the film sum waqt like soup whose ingredients are both tasty and nutritional but the final recipe somehow isn much appetizing
