1 |text really enjoyed this film because have tremendous interest american history the antebellum years and the civil war particular purchased recently from rack previously viewed videos sale the supermarket and was very glad add this one history video collection though not the caliber civil war films such glory gettysburg provides lot history the pre civil war brotherhood among cadets west point maybe the gray uniforms the youth the military discipline but fascinated the story the corps cadets from around 1830 the brink the war imagine what must have been like sit classroom with other young men learning how make war then later putting the lessons use against your own classmates actually there were two classes graduated 1861 one class may the other june the movie makes real mention this except mention henry dupont first graduate the may class and george custer last grad the june class the reason for the two classes was not much about the war but was the result switching back four year course study after few years experimenting with five year course think the first class had attended five years the other for four the movie portrays cadets were like brothers and often had nicknames for each other george fanny autie custer alonzo lon cushing james beauty stuart for stuart class 1854 etc say this film santa trail should have been because that 1940 film while enjoyable really fudges history cadets from several different classes are all graduating together jeb stuart and george custer are portrayed the best friends and are side side stopping john brown 1859 insurrection harper ferry fact stuart and custer were never friends but enemies during the war they faced each other for the first time think gettysburg 1863 stuart was the harper ferry raid but custer was still cadet the point when took place fanny custer plays role class though his classmate chums dev neill and shelby peyton are fictional believe they are respectively based partick henry rorke and john pelham two people you can look anyway truly enjoy this film any film which provides window into mid 19th century america
