1 |text must admit this one favorite horror films all time the unique way that john carpenter has directed this picture opening the door many mock genres will chill you the bone whether your first time watching your fiftieth the sound the menacing horror michael meyers and the infamous scream jamie lee curtis gives this film instant cult status and great start for the independent era love the music love the characters the familiar yet spooky setting the simplistic nature the villain and the random chaos all there really rhyme reason the killing this first film giving taste michael true nature insane some way just very brilliant beast that question may never truly answered but carpenter gives his 100 and more devotion this amazing masterpiece john carpenter the master horror while lately his films have not been the caliber that they once were see ghosts mars halloween began his powerhouse career this his ultimate film while did release other greats will always remember this one the film that caused turn all the lights beware when babysitting and check behind closed doors because you never knew where the evil would appear next carpenter has this amazing ability bring you into the world which weaves with the power his camera places these images meyers places you least expected while giving you the perception the murderer right next you loved every scene which panned back and there was michael watching from the distance without anyone the wiser that was scary yet utterly brilliant loved the scenes which carpenter pulled your fright from nearly thin air there you would minding your own business when suddenly that horrid mask would appear out nowhere like the characters you too thought was just trick the eye but that where carpenter gets you isn michael isn ghost human being least think yet has stronger mental ability than most the main characters this leads into some really dark themes and unexplored symbolism but even without that this spooky film then you just didn have enough michael just vaporizing the windows your house carpenter adds that chilling theme music still have that tapping the piano keys mind constantly wondering meyers looking through the window carpenter has found the perfect combination visual frights and chilling sounds foreshadow what may happen our unsuspecting victims next lethal and done with refreshing originality and more unique thrills than anything released today horror hollywood could muster carpenter halloween breath fresh air the midst what could rough horror year with actual scares being replaced paris hilton you know that the quality isn quite the same finally would like say that even the simplistic nature the opening murder this film terrifying and chilling the use the clown mask sent shivers spine the way that was filmed with that elongated one shot using the child mask were our own eyes still one the best horror openings ever completely sets the tone for the remainder that film you have the babysitter theme you have the childish behavior which carries with michael throughout the film and you have the art talent carpenter all rolled into one could literally speak for hours upon hours about this film but instead would rather watch again worth the repeat visit many times overall think this one the most outstanding films cinematic history skip all those foreign films that think that they are going chance the face movies leave budget tight carpenter and the slasher film genre this singular movie redefined whole generation horror films and still continues influence modern day horror treats the lethal combination genuinely spooky murderer the powerful cinematography the events which normally doesn amount much horror films and the beauty jamie lee curtis exactly what makes halloween that film above the rest sure freddy cool and you feel sympathetic for jason but michael real troubled and the loose lusting for the blood babysitters what can better grade out
1 |text number richard attenborough films director have been biographies major historical figures young winston gandhi chaplin grey owl also filmed biography historical individual but this case attenborough subject much more obscure character grey owl was canadian writer the 1920s and 1930s who promoted the ideas environmentalism and nature conservation time when these causes were less fashionable than they are today was widely believed american indian the story told about himself was that had been born mexico scottish father and apache mother and had emigrated canada where had been adopted member the ojibway tribe lived cabin lake remote part the canadian wilderness where earned living trapper toured britain twice 1935 and 1937 promote his books and give lectures conservationism and achieved great success even being introduced the royal family during one these tours attenborough then teenager saw grey owl the london palladium theatre after his death 1938 however was revealed that had not been who claimed his real name was archibald belaney and had been born the english seaside town hastings the film departs somewhat from the facts grey owl life scene set 1934 states that years old reality was born 1888 would have been that year would have been pierce brosnan age when the film was made not sure why this change was made numerous events are compressed into the last four years grey owl life 1934 1938 the film during this period that meets and marries gertrude bernard whom called anahareo reality met and married gertrude early 1925 the film also omits the fact that they were divorced 1936 and that grey owl remarried shortly before his death the revelation grey owl true identity adversely affected his posthumous reputation and was dismissed fraud his supposed deceit was even used discredit the causes which had championed richard attenborough however takes more sympathetic view his achievements one the themes explored the film the question ethnic identity although the erstwhile archibald belaney was not canadian indian birth there doubt that had deep knowledge ojibway culture and lore and that spoke their language fluently was accepted the ojibway member their tribe therefore seems unfair describe his claim native north american identity being fraudulent one merely because was identity had chosen rather than one had been born into according the film grey owl wife gertrude was herself indian descent but came from family which had been assimilated into white canadian culture her marriage can therefore seen her reclamation her family original cultural heritage she was clearly influenced her husband but she also had influence him persuading him give his work fur trapper she had moral objections killing animals for their fur one criticism made the film that pierce brosnan miscast the hero criticism which seems rooted the preconception that brosnan can only play action heroes the james bond mould seems however that brosnan may deliberately have taken this role order avoid being typecast the taciturn backwoodsman grey owl being about far from the suave sophisticated agent bond one can get the original bond sean connery also seems have deliberately opted for contrasting roles when appeared films like the hill the molly maguires brosnan fact very good this role although would agree with those who found annie galipeau weak gertrude another frequently voiced criticism with which would not agree that the film boring certainly not action film like the bonds nor great epic biopic like gandhi and may indeed seem boring those who were expecting either the one the other however likely please anyone with interest the early days the conservationist movement the philosophical implications national and ethnic identity the scenes the canadian forests are also beautifully photographed richard attenborough has done service helping revive interest this half forgotten but fascinating figure
