1 |text then you must see this film understand the reality having read the book duke now advocate for those afflicted with bipolar disorder formerly labeled manic depression hard believe that this day and age people still critique others with emotional problems those who seek psychiatric help regressive and discriminatory thinking still exists and this unfortunate this film the audience sees the pain and suffering duke had been through especially child many may remember her from the teenage patty duke show she was household name america age you learn her exploitation the ross well played howard hesseman she was growing the 1950 the stigma was full force however see she advances her career yet the illness becomes worse she goes through bouts substance abuse and promiscuity even marries someone whom she divorces the next week and she has several conflicts and tantrums with her children and elderly mother all these problem occurred before she received adequate therapy and medication recent survey released nami national alliance mental illness recorded that majority adults fail recognize most the classic symptoms bipolar disorder also was released that one five respondents the poll believed that people could control their illness without medication they wanted magazine winter 2006 you watch this film you will learn the true story talented woman who could not pull herself her bootstraps and get well until she was educated about her disorder and received proper treatment thank you duke for being advocate against ignorance and prejudice
