1 |text the story the untouchable who acted like great soldier saving the lives hundreds not thousands told the 1939 film gunga din based loosely the rudyard kipling poem the film brilliantly directed george stevens and stars cary grant douglas fairbanks and victor mclagen the title role played sam jaffe well known era ben casey boss zorba name that became synonymous with big out control hair say zorba hair anyone generation and they know what you talking about set india the time the british occupation three soldiers two romantic dashing figures grant and fairbanks and mclagen big lug are cut ups reality three overgrown boys gunga din the water carrier treated somewhat meanly verbally anyway mcchesney mclaglen but cutter grant fond him when catches din pronounced deen practicing being his soldier walk and salute apes the unit during their maneuvers cutter gives him few pointers the merry band musketeers going break when ballantine fairbanks announces about married lovely young woman joan fontaine and leaving the service however when gunga din and cutter run across thugees murderous cult led guru eduardo cianelli gunga din escapes warn the unit and ballantine insists enlisting help save cutter buddy movie after all gunga din starts out lightheartedly with slapstick and wonderful broad comedy particularly cary grant who quite funny both and fairbanks are handsome hard decide which one look first much the film made huge action sequences which are very exciting the last part the story becomes very dramatic and culminates tense thrilling battle grant has the showiest role fairbanks the lovesick romantic and mclaglen mcchesney mostly due his treatment gunga din the most unlikeable character although one detects his soft heart his love for his elephant annie his softness comes through toward the end the movie particularly the very touching tear jerking final scene always gentle and likable actor sam jaffe gives beautiful performance gunga din simple brave man with big smile powerful imagination and lofty dreams without much dialogue jaffe conveys gunga din soul magnificently this truly the ultimate adventure film massive scope with good acting rousing scenes wonderful musical score and some beautiful cinematic images another one from that remarkable year 1939 highly recommended
