1 |text rumour has that around the time that abba xc2 x96 the multi award winning swedish disco favourites xc2 x96 star had reached its zenith the band grew disillusioned with singing english and yearned perform their native tongue soon after problems began emerge the onetime wed locked watertight partnership and recordings became less and less frequent the band dissolved albeit unofficially 1982 and pop lost one its most celebrated artists although they have never admitted that there any truth those rumours the fact remains that abba would never have been successful had they only recorded their native tongue you want appeal the largest money making media market the entire world then you must cater for english speaking audiences amazing for how such small island that located stone throw away from the european continent could have created perhaps the most recognised although not most widely spoken language the world everyone speaks little bit english whether simply hello common swear word you find english speaker almost everywhere pedro galindo obviously didn agree because trampa infernal was never subtitled for global consumption until was released recently budget dvd that real shame because actually decent slasher movie that lot better than many its english speaking genre compatriots the film launches the somewhat unfamiliar territory pistol duel two unidentified characters are shown sneaking around dilapidated complex searching out one another for the inevitable final showdown after some suspense and couple near misses one the pistoleers emerges victoriously next learn that they were only paintball guns and the two competitors are actually youngsters from the local town nacho and mauricio are fiercest rivals and mauricio always trying prove himself better than his soft spoken opponent but yet hasn succeeded later that night whilst the victorious gunslinger celebrates his triumph with his girlfriend alejandra and his buddy charly mauricio enters the bar and says that has one last challenge for his glorious nemesis says that this will the competition that will prove the town once and for all who deserves the uttermost respect nacho first reluctant because alejandra warns him the perils continual competitiveness but eventually succumbs the weight peer pressure and agrees much the distaste his morally superior partner they plan head out the remote region filo caballo because recent press coverage has reported that numerous people have been butchered what locals believe vicious bear mauricio proposes that whoever murders the animal can regarded the greatest and also promises that will the last battle that wages against his adversary after visiting the armoury stock weapons and ignoring the warnings the elderly store keeper the group set out the remoteness the secluded woodland hunters become hunted they learn that the bear actually homicidal vietnam vet who still unaware that the war has ended and considers all humans his enemy what started competitive adventure suddenly becomes battle for survival they are stalked and slaughtered the malevolent assassin picked trampa whilst studying madrid from mexican student who lived the dorm room next door remember that the copy watched was faulty and the tape ended about minutes before the final credits rolled which meant never got see the final scenes thankfully came across the budget dvd recently amazon and immediately added collection gallindo slasher surprisingly good effort that excels from its skillful direction and enthusiastic plot which attempts cover areas not usually approached slasher movies fact good that reminded more than one occasion the arnold schwarzenegger classic predator this especially evident the scenes that show the creepily masked assassin jogging through the forest and stalking the panic stricken troupe they struggle escape the maniac playground despite gallindo obvious awareness genre platitudes the bogeyman even uses claw fingered glove freddy kruegar trampa also attempts add something different the standard template whilst the majority the runtime plays the concrete rules the category the final third heralds significant step individuality the maniac arms himself with machine gun and entices the hero his lair for the final showdown from here the film rapidly swaps genres and becomes almost action film which depending your taste will either excite disappoint you the last slasher that tried crossbreed the two styles was that shoddy eighties entry the majorettes which not necessarily good thing the case with many latin films especially spanish flicks almodovar and amenabar trampa has subtle undercurrent moral its story which conveyed successfully without being rammed down the viewer throat over indulge the temptations competitive masculinity and you may not always the winner sugar coated point but handled delicately enough not detract from the fun the feature trampa may cheesy but deserves seen and recognised one the better late slashers the killer looks great creepy army fatigues and white valentine style mask and the attempts originality just about work may lack the gore that most sincere horror fans enjoy but has enough terms suspense and creativity warrant least one viewing
