1 |text kim patricia clarkson george jake weber and son miles erik per sullivan are headed the country for winter weekend relief from manhattan bustling metropolis the way they hit buck and end stuck the snow group hunters who were tracking the buck come along rather than helping least one the hunters otis john speredakos mad because the accident cracked the buck antlers george kim and miles are disturbed otis and even worse quickly learn that otis has learned where they staying meanwhile miles given wendigo kind indian shape shifting spirit monster token indian whom only has seen otis psycho out get our heroes are there wendigos the woods can see where wendigo would have number problems appealing viewers fairly low budget film with technical limitations frequently showing through much the film and maybe all not really about the titular creature and perhaps the fatal blow for many people has very ambiguous ending with number questions left unanswered you are discouraged such endings and you not like films that have aim making you think about and discuss what everything meant yourself favor and avoid wendigo personally like films like that usually prefer some ambiguity the marketing wendigo geared towards those who want quick scary creature flick where they expect grand battle with some supernatural monster who defeated the end and everything tied neatly except for opening for wendigo the monster returns but that not what this film wendigo much more thoughtful and poetic than the surface such creature flick would suggest most people heck writer director larry fessenden even has character george reciting robert frost the frost poem and george comment that frost can evoke complex imagery and atmosphere out seemingly simple things the key the film one the best things about the film its complexity way there are four different films occurring the same time thread from each character george thread isn exactly the happiest most pleasant guy the world and has some parenting problems for him the film realistic horrific descent his life going from bad worse patricia thread she looking for rejuvenation her life and family she psychologist mostly denying the problems around her hoping that they away and get better otis thread even more down his luck than george and george arrival into his life symbolizes the final crack his psychological armor and miles thread which probably the most important the film life like grand poem due his youthful innocence and interpretation the world but this horror story after all albeit one with glimmer hope and the events the film give miles poetic interpretations dark turn still when everything said and done seems the only one retaining his composure due the poetic outlook even though the film low budget there are lot well executed higher budget ambitions fessenden and director photography terry stacey find some great shots beautiful locations and created some interesting slide show like montages such the cards the indian wendigo images from the book there are also interesting more traditional montages such miles nightmare wendigo better shot and edited than many big budget films other technical aspects are good for the budget the wendigo appearance the end worked for and was appropriately ambiguous the lighting was usually good there were few times that dark scenes weren clear they could have been but seemed more problem with the film stock could have been digital instead transfer thought the performances were good and far more realistic you value that than the majority films although didn really notice the score must have been okay would have noticed with negative judgment overall wendigo very good film that deserves watched without preconceptions long you don mind having think about the movies you watch
