1 |text saps sea evidently pun gary cooper film souls sea the title aptly describes the starring team stan laurel and oliver hardy who ocean voyage soothe ollie nerves only run into escaped killer nick grainger played rychard cramer this criminal both amusing and chilling making him fine foil for the boys comedic characters despite his powerful presence cramer never upstages the boys tribute stan and ollie beguiling charisma that should since the boys are supposed the protagonists this film such the charm laurel and hardy personas that they elevate average material for saps sea has its slow spots for instance previous commentator has noted bit where doctor the delightfully flustered james finlayson tries balloon called lung tester ollie lacks punch the scenario very episodic with the first part taking place the boys apartment almost completely unrelated the second part where they off sea but the whole the film highly pleasant entertainment with sufficiently brief running time that doesn wear out welcome there certain poignancy viewing the final collaboration between laurel and hardy and producer hal roach haven seen all laurel and hardy post 1940 films but those that have seen don measure even the weakest hal roach products these later movies laurel and hardy seem alien environment deprived such colorful supporting players like finlayson and charlie hall and marvin hately and leroy shield sprightly musical scores they also aren the well meaning and optimistic bumblers know and love but the later films are either exasperating blockheads pathetic misfits pity that many hal roach laurel and hardy films are now generally unavailable the public even minor entry like saps sea one can see that laurel and hardy were great comedians this was because hal roach for the most part allowed stan laurel the guiding force behind the team complete artistic freedom once laurel lost his autonomy other studios the team lost much its uniqueness
