1 |text true that danny steinmann the unseen simplistic horror thriller with very predictable plot particular attempts for twists surprises whatsoever and featuring literally every single clich xc3 xa9 the genre has brought forward over the decades but that doesn necessarily make bad film the contrary friends and were pleasantly surprised this obscure but nevertheless intense little shock feature that mainly benefices from handful brutal images and downright brilliant casting the beautiful and ambitious reporter jennifer fast and two her equally attractive friends travel little californian town shoot documentary the anniversary festival but their hotel forgot register their booking their search for place stay the trio runs into the exaggeratedly friendly but suspicious museum curator ernest keller who invites the girls stay his remote countryside mansion one one the girls experience that keller and his extremely introvert and submissive sister victoria hide dark and murderous secret inside their house the unseen can easily described cheap and ultimately perverse amalgamation the horror classics psycho and the texas chainsaw massacre the plot series familiar themes that became notorious and endlessly imitated due these two films like twisted family secrets the cellar voyeurism crazed inbred killers and very unappetizing treatment chickens still don consider these negative remarks the unseen completely unpretentious and modestly unsettling thriller that clearly never intended the greatest horror classic the decade although the denouement the plot pretty clear quite fast director steinmann attempts maintain the mystery keeping the evil present the house unseen like the title promised the casting choices and acting performances are truly what lift this sleeper above the level mediocre sydney lassick immortalized since his role the overly anxious psychiatric patient charley cheswick one flew over the cuckoo nest truly the ideal choice for the role ernest keller his persistent friendliness and almost naturally perverted appearance are exactly what the character needed also stephen furst who eventually turns from the unseen into the seen gives away tremendous performance junior looks and acts like authentic handicapped man and his attempts get close jennifer the basement are genuinely unnerving the unseen slow and predictable but nevertheless potent early film that will certainly appeal fans exploitation and generally weird stuff
