aria fantasising about blowing the mansions and stately homes the rich capitalists who killed him antonioni challenge his audience pick the guns pickets and explosives says tear the walls down before they cage you course the film had effect its audience they recognised zabriskie point being just another self centred commercial attempt being radical sort commodified radicalism felt untruthful and tame thematically the film pretty stupid antonioni basically says that you are unhappy with the modern world and the fat cats who exploit you you should either flee the desert mark actively fight the system daria that all well and good but though artists constantly warn such dystopian nightmares they all mostly unable show how effectively administer change like the end fight club nihilism and violence achieve nothing the real world social change tends instigated humble inventors spurred ahead minor technological advancements mean what liberated women more than contraceptives very bad film the problem antonioni does not really believe rebellion quiet and contemplative man introvert who seems have made extroverted film simply garner more adoration from the counterculture who embraced his earlier film blow such zabrinskie point comes across very pretentious and stupid film essentially year old man say look daring rebel there are many films which the audience encouraged fight the system but they all fall into one four categories the first category you have films like network cool hand luke cuckoo nest and spartacus these all show that the lives freedom fighters all end failure though each case the spirit revolution survives the message that you can not effect change but dying failing the optimistic notion change survives through martyrdom essentially must keep failing rather than give hope then you have films like fight club zabriskie point and falling down which simply encourage you explode tear all down blow all everything lie you might well out guns blazing these films are borne out angry reactionary feelings rather than any sort common sense then you have the flight rather than fight category terrence malick and antonioni are the masters this genre films like the passenger red desert and badlands show human beings running from worlds they not like and forging islands peaceful havens for themselves both directors are pessimists that malick has his islands destroyed and antonioni has his islands offering sense happiness solution then you have the fourth category films like donnersmarck the lives others ashby bound for glory and kubrick clockwork orange treat artists force change and rebellion these dystopian worlds which everyone content slave the state the unbridled creativity and freedom will the artist criminal who keeps the system check simply existing outside the herd you create waves your comments actions and critical eye challenges the status quo such donnersmarck film has novelists and artists undermining nazi germany whilst kubrick has alex the artist criminal fighting nazi droogs painting the town blood and sperm
