1 |text this was basically attempt the same thing with batman that was done with gilligan island surviving gilligan island for those you who missed and shame surviving gilligan island full title surviving gilligan island the incredibly true story the longest three hour tour history was special from few years back where bob denver gilligan dawn wells mary ann and russell johnson the professor related the story the show creation cancellation rediscovery rebirth along the way stories were dramatized with actors portraying the original cast and crew was very well done was funny well cast and came across genuine document the show return the batcave the misadventures adam and burt similar style the telling the history the show the enactments the general feel are all the same what missing the straightforward approach that surviving took return adam west and burt ward both receive invitations car show which they were not meant invited after being allowed stay adam and burt witness the theft the centerpiece the show the legendary batmobile adam and burt decide chase after themselves leading them through clues that cause them think about the history the show this eventually leads the revelation who stole the batmobile and why choosing use this conceit actually having plot the biggest letdown this show unlike surviving return forces the viewer follow less interesting storyline the theft the batmobile instead focusing all its attention what the audience would most interested the history the show the historical sections that work the best the casting surviving excellent jack brewer adam west and jason marsden burt ward capture the feel the actors without looking too much like them brett rickaby frank gorshin bears stronger resemblance his subject but captures none the late gorshin charm only his characterizations other actors portrayals are short and functional with none standing out especially good bad many the stories have been told before but they mostly play out amusingly with only the occasional clunky presentation another wonderful bit from the historical sections was the use audition footage lyle waggoner tryout for the part batman the only place where the flashbacks fail when they insert obviously made plot points advance the main story this downgrades the accuracy the flashbacks needlessly the main plot that what must call course ludicrous this not really fault and itself but just not carried off well enough cover the shortfall strong performances and good writing can make for silly plot especially these kinds things but really get neither here the performances west and ward seem somewhat flat even for them the dialog too carefully written for feel natural again think the comparison surviving gilligan island can seen that the dialog mostly just there set flashback surviving that all intends return tries double duty and unfortunately often fails gorshin and newmar well although agree with others that gorshin had not aged well and that newmar had and what waggoner taking look that good but aren given enough again think they all would have been better served more straightforward presentation than the one chosen here another odd point about return this special about the batman series and its history yet all the clips shown are from the theatrical movie even the waggoner footage technically movie footage you know you bat history then you know that the movie was originally planned made first only delayed favor the show when cbs needed fill time fast when waggoner and west were testing for the role was for the movie not the show why return only uses movie footage unclear most probably has with rights issues but distinct distraction those the know seeing julie newmar the present but only footage lee meriwether catwoman the past overall liked the show mainly for the flashbacks would have preferred the style used surviving gilligan island but can understand why they want more story oriented piece given the subject matter besides like these people nice see them out and about still having fun with one the great pieces entertainment history just wish they had done little better and when more the original cast was still alive there
