1 |text the blob great horror movie not merely because the vividly horrific images its nearly unstoppable flesh dissolving title character but because features real societal message many ways feel good horror film the clever storyline helped immeasurably solid performances from the entire cast the two romantic leads steve mcqueen and aneta corsaut bring surprising depth and sentimentality the proceedings they are misunderstood but very well meaning young people and very easy root for them this pro society movie and its juvenile delinquent characters cause trouble mainly out boredom not out some malevolent character flaw steve mcqueen drag racing rival almost appears enemy early the proceedings but quickly joins mcqueen campaign save the town from the oozing invader once sees mcqueen seriousness this way character situation that first appears cartoonish suddenly develops depth and human realism the authorities initial skepticism the kids wild claims proved wrong and once the threat acknowledged all all conflict within the society disappears this unification purpose and the validation the troublemaking teens becomes official when aneta corsaut father breaks into the school obtain the fire extinguishers needed freeze the blob any other day breaking into the school would considered act vandalism typical juvenile delinquent this particular day necessary action performed adult authority figure this turning point clear that there are lines division between the young and the old this unusual film that acknowledges the perception generation gap but suggests that more imaginary than real and that given real crisis people will naturally band together restore order the blob perfect tonic for the kind depression that generally comes with viewing night the living dead 1968 much has been made the film cheap but innovative and effective visual effects they are undeniably clever lot the gravity defying tricks see the blob perform were achieved with miniature sets designed rotated the camera was typically attached the sets very firmly locked down position the lights had similarly attached that the lighting remained steady the room was turned this way and that these scenes were often photographed one frame time the room was slowly turned the silicone blob oozed very slowly and its action needed sped way this was similar stop motion photography but utilizing blob silicone rather than articulated puppet even today the effects are startling and bizarre very good film with exploitative sounding title the blob must see
