1 |text many people know how feels when loved one lost the feelings pain grief and sorrow can unbearable however sometimes the memories they leave behind that trigger the saddest emotions this theme superbly portrayed the short film tulip directed the award winning australian actress rachel griffths described movie much about memories about love string sensitivity and sentimentality expertly threaded into this triumphant minute film tulip beautifully wrought touching and heart warming story man journey coming terms with the loss his wife through the relationship shares with very special animal tulip the film opens with rising dawn the chirping birds and vast landscape introducing the sense rustic harmony present throughout the film soft music plays marking the entrance ruth jean bain she wears flowered dress and apron with sun hat her head she gently pets tulip caressing her ears and patting her back the furnishing the house impressive and the attention detail creditable vase tulips can seen the bench reflecting the peaceful rural community will charles bud tingwell greets ruth she spooning the milk from the bucket they pour the milk and coffee together sign companionship and teamwork not word said but obvious that their relationship close and affectionate they paint perfect picture happiness sadly happiness doesn last forever the tragic passing ruth affects will deeply effective scene fading cars highlights will isolation and vulnerability the end the day the funeral soon sinks into depression and becomes oblivious his surroundings when everything seems hopeless and lost will moment despair tulip becomes the symbol ruth the genuine connection will has with his late wife was through tulip that will learns cope with the absence ruth and overcome the heartrending feelings loneliness each the characters realistically and solidly portrayed especially the part will charles bud tingwell brings the character life through personal investment the recent loss his own wife audrey tingwell effectively reflected his acting every sag his shoulder and every frown his brow make the viewer empathize strongly with the character the character ruth wonderfully carried out jean bain although ruth does not say single word throughout the movie her sweet personality and loving relationship with will are obvious lois ramsey and kati edwards give delightful performances supporting roles the friendly margaret and mary they also add subtle humor the bittersweet story anecdote from griffths childhood the story loss and discovery remarkably captured tulip beautifully shot and superbly acted this film will surely make you misty eyed triumphant feel like drinking cup milk
