1 |text this the french and belgians doing what they best quirky visually inventive exhilarating and emotionally challenging storytelling director jaco van dormael takes into the world georges down syndrome sufferer and his quest for meaningful relationship with someone just anyone this not done patronising way but with great sense fun and also honesty georges interplay with corporate management guru harry dazzlingly handled shifting from comedy tragedy back comedy again with breathtaking ease the eighth day puts similar hollywood fare like barry levinson oscar winning rain man robert zemeckis forrest gump well and truly the shade times evokes the humour milos forman one flew over the cuckoo nest with shades dennis potter thrown for good measure the emotionally blunted and desperately lonely yuppie harry daniel auteuil turns yet another sublime performance but matched the brilliant pascal duquenne georges movie with uniformly strong performances and many memorable set pieces the shoe shop scene car showroom scene george dance genesis jesus knows the conference scene the fireworks scene you haven seen there only one thing just rent attend screening retro cinema near you and see what you been missing better still buy this movie sheer genius
