1 |text canadian director kari skogland film adaptation the margaret laurence novel the stone angel ellen burstyn hagar shipley proud and cantankerous woman approaching her nineties who wishes remain independent until the very end stubbornly refusing placed nursing home her well meaning son marvin filmed manitoba canada and set the fictional town manawaka the stone angel straightforward and conventional interpretation the book that has been required reading canadian high school english classes for almost half century the title the film comes from the stone statue erected hagar mother grave which serves metaphor for hagar inability express emotion during her tumultuous lifetime burstyn brings vulnerability and humor the role but bit too likable fully realize the ego driven self defeating character who managed alienate her wealthy father her well meaning but alcoholic husband and both her sons she nears the end her days she reflects that pride was wilderness and the demon that led there was fear was alone never anything else and never free for carried chains within and they spread out from and shackled all touched confronting having spend her last days nursing home hagar looks back her life and looks her failed relationships her recollections shown flashbacks without voice over narration the story begins with dance that she attended young girl chaperoned her aunt dolly she meets her future husband the previously married bram shipley cole wings hauser poor farmer whose reputation the town sullied because his association with the native american population the young hagar played christine horne who exceptional her first feature role despite hagar pleading her relationship with bram rejected her cold and rigid father whose refusal attend the wedding starts the marriage off the wrong foot this exacerbated his leaving all his money the town manawaka condemning the young couple life poverty going through the motions her marriage bram hagar withdraws from social activities prevent being rejected the town upper classes when she produces two sons marvin dylan baker and john kevin zegers she unable give them the love that they need every joy might have held man any child mine even the plain light morning she reflects all were forced standstill some break proper appearances xc2 x85when did ever speak the heart truth like the biblical hagar who fled the desert because she could not tolerate further affronts her pride hagar leaves manawaka live ontario but eventually returns the shipley farm the scene shifts back the present hagar runs away abandoned house near the ocean that she remembers from her childhood escape from being placed nursing home marvin and his wife doris sheila mccarthy here she meets young man named leo luke kirby who takes interest her and compels her look and take responsibility for the mistakes she made her life the stone angel pulls out all the emotional stops but never fully develops its characters the point where felt any stake the story outcome although the spirited performance ellen page john devoted but naive girlfriend and the moving final scenes bring new energy the film second half
