 and there the kind sake salesman the bike who has sweet but strange connection with the shy quiet woman and course there group gossiping ladies who squat around watering hole the middle the slum not having anything too nice say about anyone unless about something erotic with guy first note with all this how kurosawa sets the picture little post apocalyptic looking not any particular time place that until couple shots see modern cars and streets marginalized society but the concerns these people are however tragic scope meant deconstructed through dramatic force like bergman kurosawa out dissect the shattered emotions people with one scene particular when the deathly looking man who has hollow sorrowful eyes sits ripping cloth silence woman goes along with sometimes there charm and even some laughs had with these people even enjoyed maybe ironically the little moments with rokkuchan specifically with kurosawa cameo painter the street the awkward silences with the man with the facial tics but while kurosawa allows his actors some room improvise his camera movements still remain they always been patient but alert with wide compositions and claustrophobic shots painterly visions and faces sometimes with the stylization silent drama meant weeper amid these sometimes bizarre and touching stories with some them the father and son the car especially sad kurosawa lights his film and designs the color scheme his first one eastmancolor like one his paintings lush sprawling spilling times over the seams but always with some control this place not necessarily lighter like the abstract has come full throttle into the scene where things look vibrant but are much darker underneath brilliant tricky double edged sword that allows for the dream like intonations with such heavy duty drama with sweet movie score toru takemitsu also responsible for ran and some excellent performances from the actors and few indelible scenes whole fantastic career dodes den its own way minor work from the director but nonetheless near perfect its own terms which with many kurosawa dramas like ikiru and red beard holds hard truths the human condition without too much sentimentality
