1 |text jake speed film that lacks one thing xc2 x96 charismatic lead unfortunately that something that really taints the entire movie and shame because heart enjoyable action movie with witty enough script and interesting derivative premise although genesis probably can traced back the success the indiana jones trilogy xc2 x96 the film actually plays little more like romancing the stone albeit reverse not author romantic adventure fiction being led adventure character very much like one her creations adventure fiction character who happens chronicle his own adventures leading ordinary woman one his adventures when young woman goes missing paris her sister margaret played the appealing karin kopins gets embroiled with pulp hero jake speed wayne crawford and his sidekick dennis dennis christopher who both turn out real and very flawed individuals adventure that takes them into the heart civil war torn african state and ultimately into the clutches two brothers the deliciously evil sid john hurt and his ridiculously camp sibling maurice roy london that the plot xc2 x96 not labyrinthine and not complicated but the story that tells doesn require great depth the action sequences are appealing begin with and certainly true that the heroic trio are put through their paces whether caught battles between government and rebel forces being dropped into pit full lions and there are certainly some quite funny lines however the film does seem struggle find ending and unfortunately the action sequences that are quite appealing begin with nowhere and ultimately become bit bland and irksome this however may not have been such issue was possible like jake speed but due wayne crawford performance becomes harder really care what happens now don know was stretching himself little thin was also the producer and writer the movie whether simply not good actor haven seen him much else but never really convinces roguish mixture doc savage indiana jones and jack colton this shame because most the other characters play their roles well xc2 x96 karen kopins funny and convincing and her character shares some nice banter with jake unfortunately never convinces dennis christopher perfect the archetypal sidekick and john hurt plays the part with camp relish xc2 x96 almost were sixties episode batman strides about his few scenes growling ridiculous cockney accent putting performance that almost belongs another film sid moriarty presented jake nemesis from number his previous adventures books but always fun watch jake speed tries channel the same fun movie spirit night the comet film produced crawford few years beforehand and almost succeeds but misses xc2 x96 which shame because jake would have been good watch few more adventures and may have been served better television series would recommend this out curiosity appeal but ultimately leaves bitter taste because most the elements were there make something genuinely good
1 |text this 1984 version the dickens classic christmas carol directed clive donner stars george scott ebenezer scrooge this time around the challenge for the filmmaker was take such familiar material and make seem fresh and new again and happily say with this film donner not only met the challenge but surpassed any expectations anyone might have had for tells the story with precision and eye detail and extracts performances from his actors that are nothing less than superlative especially scott one could argue that the definitive portrayal scrooge one the best known characters literary fiction ever was created alastair sim the 1951 film but think with his performance here scott has now achieved that distinction there such purity and honesty his scrooge that becomes difficult even consider anyone else the role once you seen scott simply put scrooge and what tribute such gifted actor able take such well known figure and make uniquely his own quite miraculous truly joy see actor ply his trade well able make character real from every word utters down the finest expression his face and make all ring true study perfection the other members the cast are splendid well but then again they have order maintain the integrity scott performance and they frank finlay the ghost jacob marley notable turn though not memorable perhaps the one alec guinness marley the film scrooge angela pleasence welcome visage the spirit christmas past edward woodward grand and boisterous and altogether convincing the spirit christmas present and michael carter grim and menacing the spirit christmas yet come david warner hits just the right mark with his bob cratchit bringing sincerity the role that measures well the standard quality set scott scrooge and susannah york fares just well mrs cratchit the real gem found here though the performance young anthony walters tiny tim heartfelt without ever becoming maudlin and simply one the best interpretations and the most real ever presented film the excellent supporting cast includes roger rees fred holywell and also the narrator the film caroline langrishe janet holywell lucy gutteridge belle michael gough poole and joanne whalley fan flawless presentation this version christmas carol sets the standard against which all others must gauged matter how many versions you may have seen watching this one like seeing for the first time ever and forever after whenever you think scrooge the image your mind will conjure will that george scott thoroughly entertaining and satisfying experience this film demands place the annual schedule the holiday festivities every home rate this one
