s not occur until the very end the finale which lawyer his wife and their young daughter are danger from former client obvious plagiarism the two versions cape fear which also take place the swamplands the american south harris characterisation sullivan bible quoting religious maniac direct imitation robert niro character the scorsese version cape fear made four years before just cause there postscript just just cause borrowed heavily from several other movies seven years later its central plot twist was its turn blatantly plagiarised the ashley judd vehicle high crimes the trouble with this style film making numbers that the resulting films are generally much less distinguished than those which inspired them the whole normally very much less than the sum the parts and just cause much lesser film than any those which were cannibalised make harris normally gifted actor but this one his weakest performances largely because not much playing character playing niro playing max cady blair underwood bobby earl the supposedly innocent young man the early scenes but unconvincing bobby earl the murderous psychopath the later ones sean connery armstrong and laurence fishburne the black sheriff are rather better but neither good enough save the film connery and harris were act together another better film the rock the following year there another problem with just cause the first half the film looks like standard liberal issue movie anti death penalty anti racist and critical heavy handed policing the second half looks more like the work die hard reactionary preaching the message that all criminals are evil bastards that the only way deal with them fry them the chair that liberal lawyers are the useful idiots the criminal fraternity and that police officers who beat suspects are commended heroes the filmmakers seem have been blissfully unaware that the plot twist casually introduced into the middle their film had the presumably unwanted effect reversing its political stance they were aware the problem they ignored suitably convoluted plot was obviously thought more important than political consistency
