th domergue and has discovered that she attracted him too although must explain her what love matter final reckless attack the cobra woman against long girl friend not one the six original offenders and thompson must throw the snake out the window the pavement below the body changes that domergue the end think skip over most the questions that the plot raises just mention one the more prosaic ones passing who paid for domergue fare from somewhere asia new york who paying her utility bills the hotel who paid for her spectacular wardrobe how come she speaks american english well what the hell going the writers and director have clearly seen some val lewton modest horror films and though not much effort has gone into this production they unashamedly stolen some gimmicks from lewton lewton the cat people for instance the woman transformed into black leopard but with one tiny exception the threat always kept the shadows and all the more spooky for most the transformations here use shadows too but unlike lewton the shadows are clumsy and unambiguous lewton also made occasional use what called buses lewton first bus was literal one potential victim hurrying alone through the dark tunnels central park with only the sound footsteps something someone following her she freezes with fright under street lamp something rustles the branches the shrubs above her she looks upward there loud wheezing shriek that makes your hair stand end bus using its air brakes stop for her the producers used least two buses this film and they amount nothing guy walking distractedly across intersection for instance and there the sudden rumble truck that almost hits him there set the shot jammed with shoe horn don much care for movies that perpetuate the stereotype serpents slimy ugly venomous and phallic matter fact snakes are slimy most are harmless and many are extraordinarily beautiful furthermore they more feminine than masculine their sinuous movements and serpentine approach goals you want rep