1 |text there are many adaptations charlotte bront xc3 xab classic novel jane eyre and taking into consideration the numerous reviews written about them there also lively discussion which them the best the short film adaptations all suffer from the fact that simply not possible cram the whole plot the novel into movie about 100 min length consequently these movies only show few parts the novel the series have proved more suitable format render all the different episodes the heroine life there are three mini series released and 2006 the 2006 version not only the worst these three but the worst all jane eyre adaptations and striking example completely overrated film the novel beautiful lines are substituted insipid and trivial ones and crucial scenes are either deleted replaced scenes which have nothing whatever with the novel what all leads then that the characters portrayed have not only nothing common with the rochester and jane the novel and behave exactly the opposite way described the book but that also their behaviour and language absolutely not consistent with the behaviour the period which the novel set silly soap opera which the actors look and act they had been put the costumes the 1850ies mistake this jane eyre dares call itself indeed slap the face charlotte bront xc3 xab the 1973 version very faithful the novel that the long dialogues between rochester and jane are rendered nearly their full length but what works beautifully the novel does not necessarily work beautifully the screen times the language the novel too complex and convoluted appear natural when spoken screen and the constant interruptions the dialogues jane voice overs add the impression artificiality and staginess and despite the faithfulness the novel the essence the scenes not captured another problem the casting the main characters sorcha cusack portrayal jane bold self confident worldly wise young woman totally odds with the literary model and michael jayston although good actor does simply not possess the commanding physical presence nor the charisma necessary play rochester although decent adaptation simply fails convey the passion and intensity the novel and never really captivates the audience all the faults the version stand corrected the mini series with timothy dalton and zelah clarke although from purist point view timothy dalton too handsome tall and lean rochester possesses the essential qualities for the role has imposing physical presence great magnetism and air self assurance and authority and despite his undeniable handsomeness looks grim and stern enough play the gloomy master thornfield convincingly but the excellence his performance lies the way renders all the facets rochester character all the actors who have played rochester the only one capture them all rochester harshness nearly insolence his moodiness and abruptness well his humorous side his tenderness his solicitude and deep frantic love dalton handling charlotte bront xc3 xab language equally superb even rochester most far fetched and complicated thoughts ring absolutely true and natural when dalton delivers them the definitive rochester unsurpassed and unsurpassable and after watching him this role impossible imagine rochester played any other way any other actor zelah clarke delivers equally excellent performance role that possibly even more difficult play well than the one rochester she portrays exactly the jane the novel outwardly shy reserved and guarded young woman but who possesses great depth feeling and equally great strength will she catches beautifully the duality jane character her modesty and respectfulness the one hand and her fire and passion the other her seeming frailty and her indomitable sense right and wrong she and dalton have wonderful chemistry and their scenes together are pure delight regards faithfulness the literary model this version also quotes verbatim from the novel does the version but with one important difference the dialogues are shortened this version but the core lines which are essential for the characterisation the protagonists and the development the plot are rendered unchanged thus the scriptwriter avoided any artificiality speech while still fully preserving the beauty and originality charlotte bront xc3 xab language and contrast the earlier bbc version the essence each scene perfectly captured the plot the novel followed with even greater accuracy than the series nearly scene for scene enactment the novel where equal time and emphasis given each episode jane life the only jane eyre adaptation that has gypsy scene worthy the novel and the only one which does full justice the novel pivotal and most heartrending scene when jane and rochester meet after the aborted wedding timothy dalton particular plays that scene with superb skill renders with almost painful intensity rochester anguish realizes jane resolution leave him his frantic attempts make her stay and his final despair she indeed leaves him heartbreaking almost devastating scene which will stay with the viewer for long time with even the smaller roles perfectly cast excellent script and two ideal leading actors this the definitive and only true jane eyre
