-1 |text prom night title only remake the 1980 slasher flick that starred jamie lee curtis and leslie nielsen this movie takes place oregon town where donna brittany snow about her senior prom and let herself have some fun after going through some extremely traumatic events the past few years she and her friends arrive the prom which taking place grand hotel and try and enjoy what supposed the most fun night their lives little does anyone know man from donna past who has haunted her for years also the prom and willing kill anyone way his pursuit her fan the original prom night tried maintain little hope this movie but have admit was quite disappointed prom night suffers from the worst affliction horror movie could have and that predictability there are absolutely surprises here and felt had seen everything this movie done dozens times often better before what does this equate for the audience boredom unless course you have never seen any horror movies are part the pre teen crowd but the majority the audience will most likely able guess nearly everything that going happen the plot simplistic but the entire script void any type surprise twist atmosphere anything and this really really hurts the movie because never really gives the audience anything sink their teeth into all just seemed very bland lot people seem complain with the fact that this slasher movie well and understand what they are saying but don think impossible make good slasher movie with minimal gore take carpenter halloween for example little screen violence but still extremely frightening and effective movie you don need gore make film scary but even had prom night been gratuitously violent which not very tame still would have added little the movie because there not much the script build begin with the tension and suspense here mild best and spent most the movie predicting the outcome situations and was correct about the time our characters aren well written enough either for the audience make any connection them and their the numbers demises are routine and careless will point out few things did like about this movie though because wasn completely useless the cinematography really nice and everything was very well filmed and fairly stylish among the jump scares that are for the most part very predictable there were few that were kind clever the sets for the movie are nice too and the hotel neat place for the plot unfold however predictable the unfolding may for the acting mediocre best brittany snow plays the lead decently but really the rest the cast doesn show off much talent johnathan schaech plays the villain and probably the most experienced performer here but even isn that impressive however did like the character played which was nice change from the typical masked stalker type killer see lot far the ending goes the last fifteen minutes the film had bored wit end and was very anti climactic overall prom night was disappointment everything was very the numbers routine and predictable which somewhat upsetting considering this had the potential decent slasher movie there were few neat moments but the movie lacked any suspense atmosphere and had little plot development nor believable characters advise seasoned horror fans save their money and wait till out video rent the original instead because there are absolutely surprises here some may find little entertainment but was far too predictable for tastes expected better and left the theater very disappointed
