1 |text way way back the 1980s long before nafta was drafted and corporations began shed their national identities the united states and japan were each other throat the world manufacturing race remember sayings like union yes the japanese are taking this country over and americans are lazy the reagan era winded down and corporations edged towards global marketplace director ron howard made one several trips into the comedy genre with his 1986 smash gung which drew over million box office receipts while many ways dated howard tongue cheek story colliding cultures the workplace still offers hard truth for industrial life today gung focuses hunt stevenson michael keaton the automakers union rep from hadleyville small depressed town the foothills pennsylvania stevenson has been asked visit the assan motor company tokyo similar real life toyota which considering operation the town empty plant with hundreds residents out work and the town verging collapse assan decides move and stevenson hired liaison between company officials and workers the assembly line the 112 minutes gung humorous look these two sides with their strengths and weaknesses equally considered one hand american workforce that values its traditions but often caught the frenzy pride and trade unionism the other hand japanese workers who are extremely devoted their job yet lacking personal satisfaction and feelings self worth stevenson find american working class figure average intelligence with the skills chat people through misunderstandings with the survival his workers jobs and most hadleyville the line stevenson proves likable guy who wants nothing more than fair chance although his cleverness will sink him into great deal trouble besides answering the heads assan witness delicate balancing act between stevenson and his fellow union members many whom grew with this includes buster george wendt willie john turturro and paul clint howard ron brother the japanese cast headed gedde watanabe also known for sixteen candles and volunteers watanabe plays kazihiro the plant manager who down his luck and begins feel sympathy for american life constantly shadowed saito sab shimono the nephew assan ceo who desperate take his spot the pecking order while given light touch these characters fare very well conveying ideas the japanese working culture with hunt stevenson dominating the script michael keaton has give solid performance for this film work gung indeed slam dunk success for keaton who also teamed with ron howard 1994 the paper made this film during string lighter roles that included mom beetle juice and the dream team before venturing into batman one good cop and life also hard not like gedde watanabe performance the odd man out who first wears japanese ribbons shame before teaming with stevenson make the auto plant cohesive unit the supporting cast top notch including wendt turturro shimono and soh yamamura assan ceo sakamoto mimi rogers supplies romantic interest audrey hunt girlfriend edwin blum lowell ganz and babaloo mandel teamed for gung solid writing the incidental music which received bmi film music award was composed thomas newman gung soundtrack songs are wall wall 80s including don get wrong tuff enuff and working class man the success gung actually led short lived series abc while more impressive social commentary twenty years ago ron howard film still has its comic value available dvd part the paramount widescreen collection and tad short changed audio options are provided english surround english dolby surround and french dubbing but subtitles are english only there are extras not even the theatrical trailer the plus side paramount digital transfer quite good with little grain after the opening credits and high quality sound while few extras would have been helpful especially that gung was box office success there little complain about the film presentation itself out
