1 |text the write word what you see what you get not really what madhur bhandarkar brave and brilliant page does destroy the myth attached the glam and glitterati that colour the pages our newspapers and whose lives read party habits follow with such maniacal fervour which only our intrinsic voyeuristic streak can explain the page phenomenon deplorable enigmatic how exactly did gain such control over the printed word and when did start encroach into the front page subject for another debate bhandarkar cleverly avoids that concerned only with the mechanisms this grotesque existence and doing that pieces together the various elements this way life like robert altman although not comparing bhandarkar altman genius bhandarkar uses myriad characters further his motive whether page wannabe nri the gate crashers the newly rich upcoming model socialite politician erotic novella authoress all the characters are introduced with objective and each them has separate character sketch even their parts may miniscule and therein lays the film appeal konkona sen sharma plays madhavi sharma young and talented journalist who covers page for nation today initially content with her job she soon begins see the ugliness this underbelly that covered its fake and cosmetic profligacy but bhandarkar resists the temptation make this subject into moral policing movie and avoids concentrating one character alone hence the movie not only about madhavi but also equally about deepak suri boman irani madhavi editor who passively accepts his role cog larger machinery anjali thapar soni razdan socialite suffocating from the social pollution abhijeet rehan engineer homosexual make artist and madhavi roommates pearl sandhya mridul the sassy airhostess and gayatri tara sharma aspiring actress seems like impossible task assimilate many characters and more one story but full credit nina arora and manoj tyagi for penning tight screenplay the dialogues sanjeev datta and bhandarkar have been written with great attention detail any narrative matter how good can fall flat with the lack genuine performances thankfully page brims with actors and not stars konkona goes through her author backed role with effortless ease ditto boman sandhya mridul gets the best written part but almost overdoes atul kulkarni wasted though with underwritten character times the director seems too keen incorporate much possible paedophilia homosexuality etc but the contexts which they are used not make them look rushed ultimately bhandarkar attempt satiate our voyeurism but takes step further takes inside the photographs and exposes the gruesome realities this sect humanity that strangely seems living different and remote world these are the same people that indulged new year revelry while few hundred kilometers away their fellow countrymen had been ravaged nature ferocity clever writing skillfully incorporated songs able performances and genuine feeling sincerity are what make this film worthy spite its lack finesse and poor production values page optimum way enter new year cinema abhishek bandekar rating poor average good very good excellent 29th january 2005
