1 |text you know you for something different when movie has christopher walken playing the part professional hit man and isn even one the bad guys although could with some judicious trimming here and there man fire generally effective crime drama that ranges tone from the openly sentimental the downright brutal and just about every tone imaginable between denzel washington stars creasy former cia assassin who has recently quit the business and seeking some sort redemption for the sins committed far been looking for answers bottle and the bible and not doing all that well with either the movie opens mexico city has been ravaged series kidnappings aimed the powerful and well possibly perpetrated the very police force assigned keep law and order the community creasy accepts the position bodyguard the daughter wealthy business owner who rightly fears for her safety the first third the film devoted the growing friendship between creasy and his charge pita sweet little girl who slowly but surely works her way into creasy initially hardened heart and affections the last two thirds the film turns into avenging angel melodrama creasy systematically seeks out and eliminates all those responsible for tragedy that occurs early the story based the novel quinnell man fire astutely written brian helgeland and flashily directed tony scott coolly efficient action picture that never shies away from the raw brutality its subject matter takes risk asking identify with man who for all intents and purposes achieving his redemption torturing and murdering admittedly disreputable people these scenes carnage and violence are both intense and suspenseful even they times border the exploitative even better are the quiet intimate moments between creasy and pita the early parts the movie washington and the wonderful dakota fanning establish natural easygoing rapport that helps set the stage for the chaos and turmoil follow washington carries the movie with his quality stoic righteousness making understand his character emotional level even what doing eludes intellectually addition the two leads there are solid performances from walken marc anthony radha mitchell mickey rourke rachel ticotin and giancarlo giannini but washington and the delightful fanning who steal the show man fire would have been better with about half hour taken out its running time but this still better than average crime thriller
