1 |text locataire the tenant without doubt one the most important horror movies ever made polanski stars trelkovsky timid file clerk living paris who answers advertisement for apartment only find that the previous tenant attempted suicide leaping from the apartment window trelkovsky compelled visit her the hospital and there meets stella isabelle adjani trelkovsky immediately moves when the previous tenant dies and first quite pleased with having found such nice apartment his happiness soon replaced waves paranoia becomes increasingly suspicious his neighbours who seem trying provoke trelkovsky into repeating the previous tenant suicide this film great polanski manages create surreal atmosphere dread and paranoia plenty brilliant moments such the classic scene where trelkovsky discovers the previous tenant tooth hole the wall the fever dream where wanders into the building bathroom find the walls covered with hieroglyphics the photography sven nykvist truly beautiful the tenant neglected gem may difficult track down but more than worth the effort
1 |text first glance would seem natural compare where the sidewalk ends with laura both have noirish qualities both were directed otto preminger and both star dana andrews and gene tierney but that where most the comparisons end laura dealt with posh sophisticated people with means who just happen find themselves mixed murder where the sidewalk ends set completely different strata these are people with barely two nickels rub together who are more accustomed seeing the underbelly society than going fancy dress parties where the sidewalk ends gritty film filled with desperate people who solve their problems with their fists some other weapon small time hoods are dime dozen and cops routinely beat confessions out the crooks getting caught murder investigation seems natural breathing while haven seen his entire body work based what have seen dana andrews gives one his best performances the beat down cop det sgt mark dixon the kind cop who used roughing the local hoods gets him information confession one night goes too far and accidentally kills man does his best cover but things get complicated when falls for the dead man wife morgan taylor tierney whose father becomes suspect number one the murder case morgan father means the world her dixon got what can clear the old man without implicating himself technically where the sidewalk ends outstanding besides the terrific performance from andrews the movie features the always delightful tierney she has quality that can make even the bleakest moments seem brighter the rest the cast just solid with tom tully the wrongly accused father being real standout beyond the acting the direction sets lighting and cinematography are all top notch overall amazingly well made film have one complaint and admittedly very very minor quibble that tierney almost too perfect for the role and her surroundings little difficult believe that woman like that could find herself mixed with some these unsavory characters not really her fault just the way tierney comes across she seems little too beautiful polished and delicate for the part but her gentle kind trusting nature add sense needed realism her portrayal
