1 |text acidic unremitting and beautiful john schlesinger masterpiece less effective today than years ago when american life was even more disorienting the film probably could not have been made any other time history because many upheavals were taking place the late 1960s final dissolution the great american west the intensification war vietnam and the clash social ideals that were bewildering variety midnight cowboy widely known the only academy award winning film garner rating but there much more behind its fame also exceeds the norm work art while this film from the novel james leo herlihy has much say about the erosion american life transcends 60s politics looking into the hidden bonds friendship and dealing with themes familiar man all eras the two main characters fact are standard antiheroes men who have nothing grand offer but plenty vent about our world the initial focus midnight cowboy year old joe buck physically imposing texas native played jon voight the opening scenes follow joe bus trip new york city where plans using one his few genuine talents the ability pleasure women and earn his fortune hustler learn upon his arrival that joe laughably xc3 xafve the sex trade garbed cowboy duds and proclaiming himself one hell stud the young texan flounders through his early tricks before partnering with enrico ratso rizzo dustin hoffman sickly con man and petty thief from the bronx ratso who short thin and with limp proves little monetary help joe they quickly run out cash and life grows severe the winter months joe and ratso shiver condemned manhattan apartment building with hardly dollar square meal their names over this period that strong friendship develops between them the two men relying each other battle tremendous odds throughout the film joe hearkens back earlier years texas including life with his grandmother sally ruth white who served guardian his harried relationship with crazy annie jennifer salt notorious local girl and traumatic event which joe and annie were assaulted town folk who wanted break the love affair very much its time midnight cowboy strings together wild array flashbacks dream sequences and psychedelic imagery that shed light the main characters while also distorting their backgrounds for every moment understanding gain from joe and ratso more questions about their lives are generated both men are doubt tatters they have clear sense direction until ratso falls into the throes illness and joe finally senses purpose for being alive this revelation pushes midnight cowboy its conclusion rather hopeful one very grim story while joe and ratso badly need some luck the direction john schlesinger clearly outlined and uses the gritty atmosphere waldo salt screenplay allowing voight and hoffman thrive their interactions look extremely natural and the supporting cast which features sylvia miles brenda vaccaro and members the andy warhol clique offers itself essential part the storyline the flashback sequences involving voight ruth white and jennifer salt are particularly impressive dealing with the heartbreak time lost any young person wondering about the psychedelic era advised watch this film thanks the excellent cinematography adam holender the boy who could fly smoke and editing hugh robertson shaft the visuals midnight cowboy work with its soundtrack assembled john barry cohesive unit sometimes foreseeing music videos the past two decades the lead song everybody talking sung nilsson which was actually used temporary track during the editing phase the memorable harmonica theme played jean toots thielemans midnight cowboy has been released two disc collector edition mgm which contains expanded features and commentary also available 1998 dvd release used for this review which offers dual widescreen and standard format with dolby digital sound enhancement three language subtitles and closed captioning french dubbing theatrical release trailer not the original advertised and eight page production booklet both dvd editions contain 25th anniversary restored version the film showing its original brilliance well deserving its three oscars best picture schlesinger waldo salt and additional nominations voight hoffman sylvia miles hugh robertson midnight cowboy will sure hold its place the list immortal classics xc2 xbd out
