1 |text pickup south street high speed drama about small time criminal who suddenly finds himself embroiled the activities group communists the action presented very direct and dynamic style and the momentum kept means some brilliant editing the use wide variety different camera angles and effective close ups also contribute the overall impression constant motion and vitality samuel fuller style directing and the cinematography joseph macdonald are excellent and there are many scenes which through their composition and lighting produce strong sense mood and atmosphere ace pickpocket and repeat offender skip mccoy richard widmark gets into deep water when steals wallet from young woman named candy jean peters the new york subway she was being used her boyfriend joey richard kiley make delivery one his contacts communist organisation and unknown her she was carrying government secrets recorded microfilm two fbi agents had been following candy and witnessed the theft one the agents continues tail her back joey apartment and the other zara willis bouchey visits police captain dan tiger murvyn vye zara explains that the fbi has been following candy for some months part their pursuit the ringleader communist group order identify the pickpocket tiger calls stoolie called moe thelma ritter who after being given precise description the cannon method working makes list eight possible suspects once tiger sees skip name the list immediately convinced that the man that they need track down and sends two detectives arrest him when skip brought into tiger office zara tells him about the microfilm and tiger offers drop any charges operate with the investigation skip flippant and arrogant clearly doesn trust tiger and denies all knowledge the theft the subway joey orders candy find out who stole the microfilm and then retrieve candy pays moe for skip address and when skip returns from being questioned tiger finds candy searching his home and knocks her unconscious before stealing her money when she recovers skip demands payment 000 for the microfilm she tells joey about skip demand and joey boss gives him gun and orders him recover the microfilm the following evening skip and candy are attracted each other and because their uneasy developing relationship that means evolves which they are able shake off the attentions the police soon becomes apparent however that resolving matters with the communist gang will only achieved more direct action the depictions skip candy and moe characters that inhabit seedy world which they are forced face considerable risks daily basis are powerful and compelling moe work police informer dependent her knowledge the people her community but also those people know what she does and any one them could seek their revenge any time she appears cunning and streetwise but also has her vulnerable side she describes herself old clock running down and saves money able have decent burial exclusive cemetery long island her belief that every buck has meaning its own leads her sell any information regardless danger friendships principles and yet there one occasion where she refuses and this proves fatal thelma ritter performance certainly merited the oscar nomination she earned for her role skip violent criminal with concern for his victims and having already been convicted three times the past lives under the constant threat being jailed for life convicted again despite this still continues with his criminal activities and strangely merely philosophical when moe betrays his whereabouts and then later even ensures that moe receives the type burial she valued highly candy hooker and someone whose activities constantly put her peril but behind her hardened exterior warmer side gradually becomes more evident widmark and peters are both perfect for their roles and like ritter portray the different facets their personalities with great style and conviction
