d which the turns zombie but continues preach libbed gibberish about the fate mankind only serves enhance the wtf factor and obliterate any hope serious resolution then there the infamous zombie head which slowly propels itself through the air jokerish skeletal grin wrought across its face say yeah know how bad this looks the characters are all utterly one dimensional you would expect but its the pseudo comical dialogue and dubbing that really prevents from taking their plight seriously having said that the first soldier die does put impressively valiant display against unstoppable zombie menace indeed this the first and perhaps only time hit real zombie agro and one the only effective scenes the film the guy who played the chief scientist has heart but talent utilising pauses his lines entirely random ends sounding like confused asthmatic the scientists screen attempts finding antidote are totally unconvincing now lets put these two molecules together there are few moments that stick out genuinely effective however early scene female protagonist explores abandoned garage upon entering room are confronted with hazy view shifting figure the corner and squirming mass the floor all shot atmospheric diffused light the silence interrupted the appearance speedy machete wielding zombie who trashes everything his wake his alarming desperation have her his sheer aggressiveness one the few moments real horror the film the before and after theme conveyed through the hotel that plays host the happenings the earliest stage the outbreak and later refuge our protagonists imbued with thick humid ambiance there scene which one the soldiers cautiously approaches boarded room that clearly houses hordes the undead and this quite tense things become more dramatic when they board themselves the hotel unknowing what lurks upstairs but this sloppily handled and not nearly effective could have been all all would say this film may just about deserve called royal screw potentially effective tropical zombie fest rather than simply through and through bad film nothing else has plenty the unintentional laughs that come expect from just about anything italian and gory from the eighties
