-1 |text edwin porter 1903 short film entitled the great train robbery bursts onto the screen with much excitement and ingenuity that one prepares blown away another pioneering early film just like melies trip the moon critics have hailed this being the film that introduced the western genre into modern cinema eyes they were right had everything from the planning the actual heist the train the murder unwanted civilian and that looming final scene that makes you realize that these villains mean business xc2 x96 was all monumental for its time from here eastwood every western filmmaker has used porter image some form another create their own story one cannot say that this film didn open the door but the struggle comes from the story itself the genre was defined porter but outside its initial excitement xc2 x96 there really isn anything grapple onto perhaps jaded the clich xc3 xa9 modern westerns and their haphazard messages but how can something clich xc3 xa9 before being clich xc3 xa9 the great train robbery seemed forced untraceable and unsurprising unlike melies porter tells very linear story robbers change the course train rob then shoot random people just prove they are the true villains and the final scene ends like any predestined film without any surprises glitches and that looming man with gun your proverbial face bland porter film boring the edition watched there was addition color near the end emphasize emotion which felt cheap and was not encouraging the filmmaker the viewer the issue remains that while important porter film has been borrowed time and time again has effect become diluted the story itself does not carry the emotional powerhouse once has unlike melies early film cannot watch this again know what has happened know there very little missing from behind the scenes and that finally just what has set out xc2 x96 simple story leading from point point point this issue not only gripe with this film but also the strongest element see such early film while was dull the fact that told such strong narrative xc2 x96 that our characters were characters with motives and drives was outstanding see era where nonfiction films seemed mainstream this broke the mold again not that jumping the prophetic bandwagon about this film xc2 x96 important film xc2 x96 just isn great film overall was eager jump into this film see where the roots the western genre were planted but was equally happy leave this film behind porter talented director and anderson obviously went very successful the created field but just wasn awe the film wasn expecting big budget effects like melies work nor was expecting duplicate trip the moon but did want see the same creativity exploration and originality felt porter played safe that can said with such early film but couldn feel the excitement our villains did their evil deeds wasn rooting for anyone and the final conclusion proved that the kitschy ness had worn off minutes after the film started was pioneering but not monumental the great train robbery has lost its space the time capsule cinema grade out
