-1 |text hollywood hotel was the last movie musical that busby berkeley directed for warner bros his directing style had changed evolved the point that this film does not contain his signature overhead shots huge production numbers with thousands extras the last few years the thirties swing style big bands were recording the year biggest popular hits the swing era also called the big band era has been dated variously from 1935 1944 1939 1949 although impossible exactly pinpoint the moment that the swing era began benny goodman engagement the palomar ballroom los angeles the late summer 1935 was certainly one the early indications that swing was entering the consciousness mainstream america youth when goodman featured his swing repertoire rather than the society style dance music that his band had been playing the youth the audience went wild that was the beginning but since radio live concerts and word mouth were the primary methods available spread the phenomena took some time before swing made enough inroads produce big hits that showed the pop charts hollywood hotel the appearance benny goodman and his orchestra and raymond paige and his orchestra the film indicates that the film industry was ready capitalize the shift musical taste the film was production only year and half after goodman palomar ballroom engagement there are few interesting musical moments here and there hollywood hotel but except for benny goodman and his orchestra sing sing sing there isn lot commend otherwise the most interesting musical sequences are the opening hooray for hollywood parade and let that lesson you production number the drive restaurant the film most interesting see and hear benny goodman and his orchestra play and dick powell and frances langford sing
