-1 |text this documentary had not been made the famous french director louis malle probably would have turned off after the first minutes was incredibly dull look very ordinary midwestern american town 1979 this not exactly idea fun topic and the film footage closely resembled collection home movies considering didn know any these people was even less interesting because was rather dull slice life style documentary wondered while watching what was the message they were trying convey perhaps was that values aren conservative you might think this was underlying message through many the vignettes such the republicans whose son was draft resister well the man and lady who thought sex outside marriage was just fine perhaps the meaning was that there was lot bigotry underlying the nice home town several ugly ideas such blaming jews for financial conspiracies anti black bigotry and homophobia all were briefly explored the small town 1979 was explored great depth and idyllic sort world was portrayed but when the film makers returned six years later the mood was depressed thanks president reagan this seemed very disingenuous for several reasons first the 1979 portion was almost the film and the final only consisted few interviews people that blamed the president for just about everything but acne what about the rest the folks this town did they all see reagan evil that their lives had become more negative with only few updates seemed suspicious second while true that the national debt doubled the intervening years did the gross national product and while malle shows 1979 very optimistic period was far from that the period from 1974 1980 featured many shortages gas sugar etc strikes high inflation and general malaise while not huge fan reagan because government growth did not slow during his administration the country general was far more optimistic than had been the ford and carter years while many the media demonized reagan popular sport the 80s the economy improved significantly and the documentary seems very one sided and agenda driven had the documentary given more thorough coverage 1985 and hadn seemed too negative believed after all everyone didn have their lives get worse this defies common sense then might have thought otherwise overall not the wonderful documentary some have proclaimed ranging from dull film 1979 extremely slanted look 1985 the way just does the film drop dead gorgeous seem have been inspired least part this film both are set similar communities but the latter film was hilarious mockumentary without all the serious undertones
