1 |text like the jeffersons good times was one the those classic american sitcoms which was never aired the not mention came out the 1970s decade where which wasn born yet but like most fans the show watched few episodes you tube and afterwards loved the evans family are headed james and florida two parents trying make ends meet and who despite their lack qualifications encourage their children who have their own aspirations life fulfil them and take their chances james was the strict but loving dad who didn dare hesitate disciplining michael and thelma should they over step the line whilst florida contrast was fair kind hearted and considerate mother and loving wife although she was many ways similar james with regards their attitudes parenthood and family values from afro american perspective the kids were just lively and entertaining the parents themselves was aspiring artist with goofy personality and crazy sense humour who would often wear multi coloured outfits and whose mite catchphrase infectious and familiar arnold jackson whatchoo talking bout willis from diff rent strokes michael was the smart alec who dreams becoming lawyer whilst sister thelma had her own dreams and hopes her verbal taunts with were mostly hilarious was the love hate relationship between brother and sister which was played out extremely well both mike evans and bernadette stanis over the seasons there were few cameo appearances made most notably from janet jackson debbie allen and young gary coleman himself actually prefer good times over say the cosby show which was 80s show because preferred the evans family over the huxtables both terms characterisation and felt tackled serious and difficult social issues way that resonated with many viewers was comedy but was also social commentary which aimed highlight the lives working class afro americans 1970s america the cosby show attempted cater the mainstream audience candy coated way the huxtables were portrayed blacks who easily assimilated themselves into upper class culture would associate whites with whereas good times contrast was much more edgier and was not afraid address themes such drug and child abuse realistic way actually found that whilst the cosby show can fun watch times lacked that bit sassiness which good times has and which made trendier and cooler the show did jump the shark during the latter seasons continued after john amos character james died freak accident reality was known the time that john had quit good times for good and his character death was written the show without john the show suffered and alas lost lot its charm still for sitcom good times ticked all the right boxes only they had shown this the during the 80s certainly would put mite rating and half
