e eyes lee get the eyes depths anguish few corny words and surprising amount bitterness expressed wounded veterans 1945 war film notes that might seem false contemporary viewer but perhaps shouldn the dated vernacular which difficult believe many today kids could think was actually ever spoken private gab dope drip gee you dumb coot dame swell guy and feeling sorry for yourself let consider the historical context and kind our judgments the time some this goofy lingo was the cutting edge real weak points the wounded veterans get together and argue with each other about how much collective future they have and the argument oversimply resolved with conclusion along the lines just because you have silver plate your head doesn mean people will think you bad person there are sometimes voice overs and silent prayers that are both unnecessary and downright unimaginative please god let him return and that sort thing well the film makers were operating within the constraints their times maybe that why the final fade shot independence hall and the inspiring strains america the beautiful swell the back none this can undo the film virtues which are considerable particularly the impact that horrifying combat scene not television that often you have chance all means catch
