1 |text dolph lundgren back detention marks dolphs first film nearly years and that following the delayed hidden agenda this film still marks improvement for dolph over his cheapie trilogy jill rips agent red and stormcatcher however this film well below the standard hidden agenda which was better almost every respect what this film does have favour from dolph previous outing sense cheesy fun the film also has rejuvenated dolph back high action role and good see dolph doing his own stunts again the films story ludicrous and prime movie material military man now teacher and his last day teaching whilst taking detention class runs into some slovakian bad guys who have taken over the school use cover for big drug deal the film has originality but movie this type you need have sense fun with all the cliches you take too seriously the audience will find little enjoy thankfully the filmmakers don take matters too seriously and along with all the action cliches you can think and the predictability this film has bad enjoyable kind vibe where the film let down miss using fairly decent budget the budget around million has not been well spent all screen with plenty carnage and big explosions but lot the shootouts lack imagination the opening action okay but after that the good moments become more sparse there are some good moments you have car careering through school hallways for example and decent shootout the beginning with plenty destruction the rest the shootouts are fairly mechanical but there plenty going onscreen for the cast hidden agenda boasted the best cast dolph has worked with ages there was good standard actors for dtv film this however has problems the actors are the most part bad the bad guys are terrible but the lead bad guy has kind enjoyable cheesiness because alex karsis plays over the top and without the hint any menace that you can laugh the pure badness the teenagers the piece are actually good but they are playing such cliched characters they all hate 