1 |text yet again early morning television proves invaluable resource for films that otherwise would never have been able track down four clock the morning stumbled out bed begin recording the informer 1935 fourth film from prolific american director john ford and excellent one that set during the irish civil war 1922 the screenplay was adapted dudley nichols from the novel the same name liam flaherty though was born the united states and most renowned for his americana pictures both ford parents were irish which explains the director decision direct the film victor mclaglen plays gypo nolan brutish but well meaning ruffian who informs old friend frankie mcphillip wallace ford order claim the xc2 xa320 reward for his girlfriend katie margot grahame when frankie killed during his attempted arrest the irish republican army which both frankie and gypo were members begins investigate the traitor behind the incident every clue bringing them closer and closer the real culprit meanwhile gypo plagued with guilt for his friend untimely death and descends into bout heavy drinking that rivals don birnam the lost weekend 1945 its excessiveness gypo drowns his sorrows copious volumes alcohol trapped vicious little circle depression his extravagant spending captures the attention the investigating ira members for the one time his life gypo finds himself surrounded admirers including amusing kerrigan who enthusiastically clap him the back and christen him king gypo for his physical might however obvious that these people feel affection for the man and are simple showing him attention exploit him for money the additional xc2 xa320 brought frankie death could never buy gypo assembly friends xc2 x96 indeed bitter twist irony the money was only made possible the betrayal and loss one his only good companions relatively simple fellow gypo could not possibly have fully considered the consequences his actions and eventually offered forgiveness account his not knowing what was doing but his foolishness must not unpunished criticism occasionally levelled ford film for its allegedly propagandistic support terrorist organisation though this stance obviously depends one personal views certainly don know enough irish history pass judgement there doubt that the film portrays the irish republican army selfless dedicated and impartial proud piece irish patriotism ever saw however the main theme the story that betrayal driven intense poverty one ordinary man betrays the confidence his good friend and comes deeply regret his actions the tormented gypo played mainly for pity and victor mclaglen gives powerful performance that betrays lifetime unsatisfying existence culminating one terrible decision that condemns him uneasy death the informer was john ford first major oscar success winning total four awards from six nominations including best actor for mclaglen who snatched the statue from the three way favourites mutiny the bounty 1935 best director and best screenplay for dudley nichols who declined the award due union disagreements
