1 |text okay note the people that put together these horror acting legends dvd collections truly grateful and hugely support the initiative but xc2 x85 have you even watched the films before selecting them part the collection when purchased the boris karloff collection there were several films which the star only played supportive and unessential role tower london the strange door the invisible ray however part the bela lugosi collection and here actually boris karloff who overshadows bela this actually would have been great title for the boris karloff collection instead bela lugosi character quite possibly the most good natured and earnest one ever portrayed his entire career and good old karloff actually plays the mad and dangerously obsessed scientist here the invisible ray features three main chapters the first one set janos rukh carpathian castle pretty boring and demands quite lot the viewer patience but course the character drawings and the subject matter discussed here are fundamental for the rest the film rukh karloff demonstrates couple eminent colleagues among them bela lugosi benet how managed capture extraterrestrial rays inside self manufactured device the scientists are sincerely impressed with his work and invite rukh and his lovely wife diane along for expedition the heart africa there rukh isolates himself from the group discovers the essential element radium complete his medical ray and goes completely bonkers after being overexposed the meteorite himself the third and final act obviously the best and most horrific one revolves good old fashioned killing spree with ingenious gimmicks melting statues and surprising climax karloff glows the dark and convinced the others are out steal his discovery and even his life intends eliminate them using his deadly touch the narrative structure the invisible ray sounds rather complicated but the film easy follow and entertaining the story rather far fetched but nevertheless compelling and director lambert hillyer provides several moments sheer suspense boris karloff truly fantastic and lugosi even though deserved have little more screen time their scenes together are the highlights the film along with the funky images the glowing boris
