1 |text when saw the film for the first time the early 1970s was awe this film visually was stunning and the events campuses europe and usa made you relate with what antonioni was trying say well visually the final minutes the movie blowing your mind the tyrannical establishments and big business interests the repeated blowing the beautiful house the middle desert the lead female character enjoying the natural stream cold water painting plane psychedelic designs even the staid british airways did few years ago are some the images that were copied advertising personnel all over the world for decades even pink floyd increased their fan following after the film was released you see this film some years later and you begin wonder why the same film has lost its appeal today anti establishment films have more substance facts documentation fine performances and superb screenplays antonioni seems out date flawed genius even viewing antonioni blow today gives you the similar feeling that passe zabriski point has evaluated for what was when was released was great film you were see wide panavision screen opposed the dwarfed screens the visual and aural mick jagger kieth richards pink floyd allure the film still remains the lead pair were not great actors but they were cute and natural one them mark frechette died prison usa extending the reality the non conformist values personified the film today antonioni seems out sync but watch carefully and you will appreciate the muted sounds the regular actors rod taylor spradling the ladies the swimming pool the cops the air strip the real sounds contrast are from the non conformists antonioni was relevant years ago but his grasp the medium cannot questioned even today knew what was doing
