-1 |text maladolescenza has the air dark fairy tale with its child protagonists forest setting and the discovery castle ruins yet its core the film essentially unusual psychosexual study adolescents opening with dream sequence employing the not subtle metaphor fabrizio wrestling with his menacing hound the film details his psychological persecution laura the girl who has pledged her love him and his eventual romance with the equally malicious sylvia the film psychological complexities give the film merit yet there doubting how unnecessarily exploitive the film its depiction nudity and sex the film look relies more its gorgeous locations rather than particular cinematographic skill and there doubting the film greatest asset the creepy children choir augmented soundtrack with its odd dreamlike quality the film best interesting yet pales beside louis malle surreal and brilliant black moon from the same era certainly deserving the art versus pornography debate for unlike many banned films pasolini salo larry clark ken park for instance the film rather unremarkable from artistic perspective cinema seems gradually losing its ability shock perhaps maladolescenza should admired for retaining that power thirty years after its release however shock value the one reason alone the film memorable the film does have its defenders yet does nazism
