1 |text incredible documentary captured all the frenzied chaos and misery which loomed over nyc that fateful morning september 11th intense personal and completely riveting perhaps the greatest documentary ever made accident which kind gives even greater appeal until that morning filmmakers gideon and jules naudet had been following around new york firefighter team concentrating specifically one new recruit little piece they were shooting dealing with the rigorous training become fireman out with the team that morning filming yet another simple routine cleanup jules lifts his camera the sky just time record one the only known images the first plane hitting the world trade center and from there simple documentary was more viewers are given first hand account what was like and around ground zero the amazing group fire fighters and one profoundly bewildered cameraman attempt navigate this disaster without hesitation naudet follows these automatically programmed heroes into the tower while entire support crumbles around them the raw fear unknown impending doom lurks with more viability then any fictional production could ever fathom watch less and less become audible and visible for those trapped inside nearly memorable older brother gideon candid capturing entire city the throngs larger and more palpable fear then anything they had collectively witnessed the time get see the second tower collapse the cameraman shields himself from apocalyptic debris should all but rinsing the dirt off ourselves from the amazingly close footage captured obviously the filmmakers deserve only much credit being the right place the right time document such extraordinary event though one can only admire the two brothers their extraordinary adaptation such event few desperate minutes witness them become like the firemen they document only instead saving lives they knew they had save footage even cost them their own safety after viewing and seeing that came out 2002 feel much more resentment towards oliver stone recent rendition the big budgeted world trade center many had criticized the film for ignorantly narrowing down the focus those two survivors trapped rubble and although enjoyed the movie just fine for the small and sentimental hollywood focus brought all but renders his film completely obsolete not only will this utterly gripping footage remain the only definitive collection from that day but the sublime transfer motives midway ensures that this documentary has all the heart and character needed never sensationalize the event again
