1 |text before seeing this was put off the subject matter but this not your average triumph over adversity story although this technically about blind tibetan kids climbing everest there much more this movie shows the very strong often contradictory personalities two highly accomplished blind adults leading the children erik and sabriye erik american blind mountain climber athlete and sabriye blind german academic who started school lhasa tibet they are both exceptional their own ways but disagree what will really build confidence the kids erik wants them reach the summit while sabriye wants them enjoy erik role model and take pleasure moment the nuances are complicated and one walks away not really being sure who was right the whole climb was mistake great idea the most profound scenes are with the tibetan children themselves and the hardships they faced before finding their way the school the most moving for was the story tashi frail teenager who grew the streets after his parents abandoned him could watch whole movie his life and was happy learn that thanks the school now running successful small business with some his fellow students you liked spellbound murderball you will love this
