1 |text william castle notorious among horror fans the grade director the 1950s and 60s his gimmicks his cost cutting techniques and his unique vision are legendary comes surprise then that someone jeffrey schwarz who made countless documentaries would finally take the time devote documentary his greatness such spine tingler the william castle story had general understanding who castle was having seen some his films over the years knew nothing about her personal life his goals and ambitions this film really fleshed out the man and gave fuller appreciation for the devotion had for the craft film making and his contributions the horror genre the movie depicts castle rival alfred hitchcock with hitch being the artist who wins praise while castle the carnival barker who gains cult notoriety but much less respect icon all second rate directors out there which why not surprising that john waters featured prominently here joe dante and stuart gordon also have sizable roles his gimmicks were what drove his fame and the documentary takes great pains explain them which crucial for those who are too young remember the rudimentary ghosts see separate review the buzzer the seat for the tingler see separate review money back guarantees for homicidal watching these films now outside the theater can judge them for their content which personally still enjoy but cannot fully appreciate what audiences once felt the climax the film when castle goes from cult director hollywood producer having bought the rights rosemary baby put very special place for negotiating its film release hoping direct sidelined producer order make way for new director roman polanski while first disappointed this proves one the best opportunities his lifetime hugely successful film and job excels who better control the purse wild artist polanski than penny pinching castle this was his crowning achievement though sadly the film more often connected polanski than castle the remainder his years are played out and are given personal reflections his daughter and niece across the board everyone seems have nothing but praise for the man somewhere along the way surely upset one two people but you would never know from this film and find that find this celebration bill castle life not true hollywood story fans the genre would well pick copy this work would personally recommend picking the william castle collection which has not only this but eight castle films with plenty special features even this documentary comes with audio commentary you can hear how schwarz was personally affected castle and have castle daughter terry giving running reflection her experiences with the different films and remakes almost whole new film
