1 |text pulled down vhs box from vast collection many unseen and picked out movie based the box art thought would fun and yes bad prison had that 80s cheesy look all over that box sat down and watched and and behold found that sometimes indeed sit down movie with preconceived expectations mind fortunately reversed mine quickly and soon realized was sitting down not just okay film but rather good movie total prison tells the story old dilapidated prison being reopened save budgetary concerns looks creepy all empty and filled with prisoners the prison used set incredibly atmospheric and easily the most important character the film the story using the prison its central setting tells prologue man being killed via the electric chair see lane smith guard tearing away crucifix before sending the man his maker then present day first with government board meeting deciding open the prison and send beautiful doctor make sure that conditions are acceptable she campaigned vigorously against opening the old prison then see the new warden lane smith haunted nightmare bed and given the new job opening prison has not been years well the rest follows suit prisoners and guards arrive with plenty stereotypes abounding are given some character depth and several the prisoners are interesting characters the acting better than one might expect with lane smith doing always workmanlike job viggo mortenson very different prisoner being solid tom everett tiny lister and ivan kane really exploring the boundaries their stereotypical characters chelsea field okay the female lead the best performance lincoln kilpatrick underrated character actor cresus prisoner who had been that very same prison years ago when the man had been executed with some kind terrible secret prison not the next best thing sliced bread anything like that but definitely worth look and definitely better than most would expect from was pleasantly surprised the way director renny harlin created story visually atmospheric the f