1 |text the interesting aspect the apprentice demonstrates that the traditional job interview and resume not necessarily predict teamwork skills task dedication and job performance and they certainly don reveal any hidden agendas other words good indicator potential may see job applicant action which the point the apprentice people vying for corporate position may hand over sugar coated resume and put their best personality attire for the interview but these are not necessarily the best indicator strengths weaknesses and performance briefly the apprentice involves job candidates competing for the ultimate career opportunity position real estate magnate donald trump investment company the apprentice refers the winner who will win salaried position learn the art high stakes deal making from the master himself and presumably gain prime corporate connections the position dream come true for those wanting make more money than the gnp some foreign countries entice the candidates trump shows off his private jet his private luxury apartments replete with statues and artwork his limos his connections celebrities and other aspects the life billionaire magnate the road success not easy the group divided into two teams that compete against each other each has corporate sounding name such versacorps and prot xc3 xa9g xc3 xa9 corporation the teams are assigned tasks that entail entrepreneurial venture such creating advertising selling merchandise negotiating teams select project manager who provides the leadership and organizational skills complete the task they win the manager receives lot credit particularly the eyes the final arbiter they lose the manager may also become the scape goat some the tasks are monumentally difficult with only day two complete tasks may involve creating commercial print others may involve selling retail outlet the street the tasks bring out the best and worst the participants they often show immediately who the most reliable who the most trustworthy and who hard working and the tasks also expose who not good team player who inefficient and who seems only out for themselves the tasks invariably reveal unexpected ways the strengths and weaknesses the participants and particular the project manager how well the manager communicates with the team delegates work organizes time and sets specific goals will largely determine the outcome but does not necessarily predict the winner the single most telling aspect someone potential when she assigned project manager their real abilities opposed their self propagated abilities immediately show through the veneer that cannot hidden 100 silk tie beautiful makeover leadership qualities and weaknesses often become agonizingly obvious after only few minutes those promoting themselves top notch leaders are not always strong when put into real life leadership situation always easier toot your own horn than actually engage leadership project managers even those the winning teams often not formulate cohesive strategy they often believe that diving off the deep end complete the task the first minute rather than taking little time organize and discuss how the task will completed more efficient more often than not members ill strategized team are running around like headless chickens figuring out they along and the long run they end wasting far more time the winning team gets taste the high life such eating dinner exclusive restaurant flying private jet and meeting celebrity the losing team comes the dreaded board room where trump hears the lame excuses the members and knocks off one more the contestants like pieces off chess board with the now infamous you fired often the project manager held partially responsible for the team loss and may the target trump accusatory rhetoric every week least one person becomes casualty from the losing team least favorite aspect the apprentice the board room while the tasks themselves bring out the strengths and weaknesses the candidates the board room often brings out the worst unfortunately the rules the game insist there one winning team and one losing team even the competition was close members the losing team start accusing each other often ruthlessly about who was fault and sometimes more than one person gets fired seldom see under performing candidate take responsibility for their actions the board room kristi frank and kwame jackson were possibly the only candidates who took full responsibility for her team losses and received recognition for this selfless act for kristi frank and kwame jackson had the most integrity all the candidates however trump saw kristi weak and fired her claiming she wasn standing for herself which may mean values ego more than integrity one should sacrifice their integrity for this kristi frank may not have become the apprentice but she can live with herself knowing she did not blame others unjustly isn that worth much winning the strength the apprentice also its weakness because team performance evaluated strictly winners and losers other evaluation opportunities are overlooked barring huge gaps between the winning and losing teams sometimes losing team exemplifies high standard teamwork and efficiency have seen losing teams sometimes appearing better organized than the winning team americans are often obsessed with winning and losing that often overlook excellence
