-1 |text after some internet surfing found the homefront series dvd ioffer com before anyone gets excited the dvd set received was burned amateur from home video tapes recorded off their years ago the resolution and quality are poor the images look like you would expect old recorded video look although the commercials were edited out the ending credits each episode still have voice over announcements for the segway into the abc news program nightline complete with the top news headlines from the early 1990 even with the poor image quality the shows were watch able and the sound quality was fine this show credit the casting was nearly perfect everyone was believable and really looked the part their acting was also above average the role jeff metcalf played particularly well kyle chandler most recently seen the 2005 remake king kong the period costumes were very authentic were the sets especially the 1940s kitchens with vintage appliances and xc3 xa9cor the direction was also creative and different for show that time for example conversations between characters were sometimes inter cut with conversations about the same subject between other characters different scenes the dialog the different conversations was kept fluid despite cutting back and fourth between the different characters and locations that takes good direction and editing and they made work this case started watching this series again suddenly remembered why lost interest years ago despite all the ingredients for fine show the plots and story lines are disappointing and confusing right from the start for one thing the name the show itself totally misleading when wwii ended 1945 there was more fighting obviously there was longer homefront either curiously the first episode the show homefront begins 1945 after the war had ended that like shooting the first episode gilligan island showing the castaways being rescued the whole premise the show namesake completely lost still held hope with the possibility the rest the series being flashback but the entire show takes place from 1946 through 1948 additionally this series fails miserably any attempt accurately portray any historical events the late 1940 the third episode becomes obvious that this series was nothing more than thinly veiled vehicle for ultra left wing political agenda the show set river run ohio near toledo however the show ongoing racism theme makes look more like jackson mississippi than ohio part the ensemble cast are dick williams hattie winston and sterling macer who portray the davis family much the series shows the davis family being discriminated against the evil whites the point being ridiculous and totally absurd not laughable the racism card has been played and over played hollywood now for over years get also tired having our noses rubbed daily basis the subject racism also unpopular with viewers and the kiss death for any show was for homefront the acting talents williams winston and macer were wasted their roles the stereotypical frightened angry black family the wildly exaggerated racism this series makes look like everyone ohio was kkk member something the racism issue could have been addressed this show single episode with simple punch the nose fist fight which bigot gets well deserved thrashing and leave that devoting major portion the series the racism thing gets really old really quick and its just plain stupid yet another ridiculous plot line the big boss local factory ken jenkins portrayed ebenezer scrooge like character who against pensions and raises and unconcerned about acid dripping his employees the workers revolt and take over the factory blatant pro communist propaganda message the viewer personally think this series had great potential the writers could have easily placed the timeline 1941 xc2 x96 1945 the title suggests and shown the hardships food and gas rationing and working hour days war factories course the loss brothers sons and husbands fighting overseas would have also added drama the situation was also perfect for writing special guest stars military uso personnel passing through their town during training route europe the pacific the possibilities for good story lines and plots are endless but the writers homefront david assael and james grissom completely ignored any relevant interesting plots instead they totally missed the point and strayed into bizarre and irrelevant obsession with racism and left wing politics would unfair the actors condemn the entire series but the plots and situations which they were placed are total garbage
1 |text what extraordinary crime thriller wife and saw this the toronto international film festival last week and was far and away the best movie exceptionally strong festival already second favourite film all time after strangelove and was definitely emotional high walked home and discussed the film with wife don want spoil the plot because thrillers this calibre are best enjoyed without preconceptions synopsis that feel comfortable sharing that two brothers played phillip seymour hoffman and ethan hawke are planning rob jewellery store westchester new york the film bounces back and forth time over approximately two week period time before during and after the robbery and one key scene repeated least three times ordinarily that could disrupt the momentum film but that never happens during this masterpiece the excitement the tension and even the quality the acting only seemed get better the film progressed the end was the edge seat breathlessly waiting see how would all wrap know that used few clich xc3 xa9s this post but literally was the edge seat should mention that the non linear storyline quite easy follow this isn the sort movie where you overhear audience members asking their friend explain the plot during the movie the acting absolutely brilliant all around and doubt would have the same admiration for the film the casting hadn been perfect tiny complaint that hoffman and hawke don look like brothers but that minor quibble that can easily overlook hoffman was his very best and some his scenes with hawke were positively electric marisa tomei hoffman wife and albert finney the father hoffman hawke are also very good supporting roles even some cameo performances were impressive that can still remember every remark gesture and facial expression brian byrne and michael shannon xc2 x96 absolute perfection the robbery scene felt more authentic than any other cinematic robbery scene ever watched and had the same feeling authenticity most scenes especially the ones with hoffman the music helped build the tension throughout the movie often the same notes played over very effectively had the music playing head the following day even sat through other films addition minor complaint the beginning this paragraph there was one plot twist that felt bit unbelievable major spoiler can describe the scene otherwise this film pretty darn close perfect there were about dozen great films the festival that would enjoy watching second time but before the devil knows you dead stands league its own aside the director sidney lumet spoke before the film and introduced marisa tomei and ethan hawke onto the stage tomei didn speak and she acted bit shy lumet asked can you believe that someone beautiful could camera shy that comment quite ironic considering the graphic opening scene
