1 |text this was the second two filmed hamlets the nineties the first being franco zeffirelli starring mel gibson from 1990 zeffirelli version like laurence olivier from 1948 was based upon abridged version the play with much shakespeare original text being cut have never seen tony richardson 1969 version but that ran less than two hours shorter even than zeffirelli presume that was also abridged kenneth branagh was attempting something much more ambitious film based the complete text the play with running time around four hours with his henry branagh claimed olivier crown the cinema leading shakespearean confirming his claim with his brilliant much ado about nothing rare example great film based shakespeare comedy hamlet was his third shakespeare film director also acted iago oliver parker 1995 othello and one might expect very different much ado xc2 x85 the earlier film shot villa the hills tuscany and the beautiful surrounding countryside joyous summertime film about everything that makes life worth living hamlet contrast set the depths winter the flowers the description ophelia death suggest that shakespeare himself thought the action happening summer the look the film particularly striking both sumptuous and chilly was filmed blenheim palace possibly england most grandiose stately home but also rather forbidding one the snowy exterior scenes are cold and wintry the interior ones formal and elaborate the action updated the mid nineteenth century the female characters wear the elaborate fashions that era while the principal male ones mostly wear splendid military uniforms there contrast here with zeffirelli film where both the interiors and the costumes were deliberately subdued tone the play dominated images corruption and decay branagh intention may have been contrast splendid surface with the underlying something rotten the state denmark the film notable for the large number big name actors some them very minor roles blink and you might miss john gieldgud judi dench apparently all star cast was required the production company who were nervous about four hour film some the imported hollywood stars such robin williams osric did not really come off but others like charlton heston player king billy crystal first gravedigger played their parts very well yorick normally only seen skull here seen flashback played the british comedian ken dodd brian blessed who often plays jovial characters cast against type the ghost and makes the scenes which appears genuinely frightening the major characters perhaps the weakest was kate winslet ophelia branagh leading lady his first two shakespeare films was his then wife emma thompson but their marriage ended divorce 1995 did however find myself wishing that thompson had been cast the role although winslet came into her own the ophelia mad scenes she seemed weak the earlier ones where her character still sane preferred helena bonham carter zeffirelli version richard briers plays polonius with greater dignity than often given wise and experienced counsellor rather than prating old fool julie christie also brings dignity the role gertrude there attempt here there was with gibson and glenn close the zeffirelli version suggest incestuous attachment between her and hamlet interpretation which owes more freud than does shakespeare the age difference between christie and branagh great enough for them credible mother and son which was certainly not the case with close and gibson olivier gertrude eileen herlie was bizarrely thirteen years younger than him branagh stated that his intention restoring those scenes which are often cut cinematic versions was reinforce the idea that the play about national well domestic tragedy much stress placed upon the war with norway and the norwegian prince fortinbras subplot ignored altogether zeffirelli this emphasis national tragedy perhaps best shown the character claudius sometimes played one dimensional villain there something about derek jacobi performance which suggests that claudius could have been good man under different circumstances but that allowed himself led astray ambition and lust could have been good and loyal servant his brother but chose rule bad king although tormented guilt can see way make amends for the evil has done branagh wonderfully fluent speaker shakespeare verse superb the main role like gibson has little time for the old concept hamlet indecisive passive and melancholy his active physical energetic hamlet something best shown his fatal duel with laertes his guiding principle not world weary despair but active disgust with evil and corruption was gamble for branagh make four hour epic and the film did not well the box office was however praised many critics james berardinelli being particularly enthusiastic own opinion that whatever the financial returns may have been branagh gamble paid off artistic terms concentrating the full text was able bring out the full meaning and full emotional power shakespeare most complex play when reviewed his much ado xc2 x85 said was the greatest ever film shakespeare comedy his hamlet may just the greatest ever film shakespeare tragedy
