1 |text terry gilliam fantastic twisted story virus destroying all but handful people across the earth and forcing them move underground and the man sent back time gather information about fantastic dizzying and highly stylized film that boasts bruce willis best performance ever what sets monkeys apart from most time travel sci movies that bruce willis character actually deals with what the psychological effects time travel that not knowing what reality actual reality the place that the time traveler comes from goes also the film recognizes that things that have past cannot altered and that the prevention cataclysmic event this case the release said virus cannot stopped changed willis asserts already happened while mental hospital the major dilemma the film trudges into not trite overdone plot save the world instead willis inner struggle simply survive himself fresh innovative concept and works beautifully thanks tautly written script peoples and gilliam unique brand dementia besides this monkey storytelling totally non linear and instead opts distort and bend the way the story told skillfully incorporating bevy different time sequences flashbacks dreams memories the present the past the future and even scene that lifted out hitchcock vertigo all serve envelop the viewer into its disturbing cacophony madness and futility visually gilliam master desolate umbrage and shadow rivalling tim burton his strikingly despondent scenery and imagery with cold wide and immersing cinematography gilliam plunges into the colorless surroundings and darkness his characters the scenes are often bathed strangely antiseptic dead white and help serve contrast the often veering madness characters performance wise brad pitt steals most scenes filling them with patented loony off the wall performance that deservedly garnered him oscar nomination mentioned bruce willis gives the best performance his career not reverting his heroic cliches and cardboard hero and instead portraying cole simple poignant tragic everyman equally good madeline stowe willis psychologist she holds her own injecting her character with both wild energy and strength she collapses under the weight what she comes believe false religion gilliam expert overwhelming and complex handling what could have been routine action sci film makes monkeys compelling vision nightmarish futuristic landscape its rich well thought out intricate storyline along with bravura performances from the entire cast and its brooding bleak cinematography make masterpiece madness ranking top all time monkeys darkly lavish spectacle film brimming with brilliance out
