1 |text you are looking for definitive biography the life boxer james corbett then this probably not the film for you the famed boxer receives 1940s hollywood ization his life making the story far more entertaining and engaging than real life however because the performances were good particularly errol flynn and the script likable the film embellishments can forgiven errol flynn plays gay nineties era boxer james gentleman jim corbett man who became world boxing champ 1892 the film goes from his rather humble beginnings and follows his through his career through him winning the title match against john sullivan however while could have focused mostly the matches most are rather brief the film except for the final title match and the emphasis corbett brash personality well his relationship with the lady played alexis smith throughout the film there excellent supporting work done cast wonderful supporting actors such the perennial supporting actor flynn films alan hale and the writing really helped bring these people alive what particularly nice about the film seeing the athleticism flynn boxer while few the shots are doubles almost all the boxing scenes are flynn and did convincing job pugilist this was nice departure for flynn who generally played pretty boy roles swashbucklers and this shows just how tough character was find out more about this try reading biography him was quite the rough and tumble character before coming hollywood now for the real james corbett read you aren afraid finding out how the movie isn accurate first corbett was not poor guy coming from poor family but was college educated and bright second while did get alexis smith the end the film they also divorced few years later third the wonderfully touching final scene the film between sullivan and corbett was probably the best part the film sullivan was jerk and this never could have happened reality sullivan was more the egomaniac and corbett was not the fat headed guy they portrayed the film though made for lovely film
