1 |text the young fanshawe mark letheren avid archaeologist dispatched his museum boss the large country home squire richards pip torrens where his task find provenance for and catalogue the collection antiquities and curios belonging the recently deceased father the squire the squire surprised the arrival fanshawe hadn been expecting him for another week but none the less welcomes him and gets his only servant patten david burke watson fame show him his room fanshawe must stay over for some days order finish his rather large task patten would seem not the friendliest sort and seems resent the extra work that fanshawe visit will entail the large empty house providing endless amount cooking cleaning and maintenance for him fanshawe fussy sort very neat and precise with everything having its place whether they his clothes his books and papers and rather disgusted the dirt his room needless say rather eager begin his work but unpacking finds his binoculars have been damaged transit asks the squire for replacement pair the squire who modern thinking man but also would seem rather uncultured with such matters also eager get rid the clutter around the house obliges and walks fanshawe the top the hill that can survey the estate and the surrounding villages there the squire directs him points interest including gallows hill where locals were hung for their crimes and misdemeanours his interest also taken local abbey which the squire describes ruin but fanshawe can see through the binoculars that clearly isn investigates further and pays visit the site the abbey and shocked find that there are but few stone remnants fanshawe doesn have too much time think about this conundrum darkness falls feels being watched feels presence begins see moving shadows the woods startled runs home over dinner imparts details his harrowing day the squire patten overhears the story and suggests explanation for the binoculars they used belong local man called baxter whom would seem collected bones and skulls from gallows hill boiling them for some concoction other baxter had disappeared mysteriously one night the late squire had acquired his belongings including mask made out skull and some old etchings the area these etchings fascinate fanshawe they portray the abbey seen through his binoculars but learns that the abbey had been destroyed during the reign henry vii and would impossible for baxter have drawn the sketches never the less they are signed and dated baxter the recent past concludes that the binoculars have some special power that night has horrifically vivid dreams when wakes sets off with the binoculars have closer look the abbey through them what finds surprises him but has put himself perilous danger doing fanshawe finally becomes trapped his dangerous obsession darkness falls the squire and search party search the now missing archaeologist they are alerted dozens loudly cawing crows circling above gallows hill they quicken their speed but will they time help save fanshawe from his destiny the ghost story for christmas series films made the bbc sadly ended its initial run films 1978 with the ice house they were for the most part based the work the great james 2005 and 2006 the series was revived briefly and thankfully view from hill also marked return the work james whose ghostly writings have haunted many generations readers director luke watson being new the series might have worried fans the older films but returns the period setting abandoned the later films which immediately sets the tone for great ghost story his direction assured stays true the mood the masters works and gradually builds the fear factor terrifying climax all the while keeping what the viewer sees minimum thus upping the tension and mystery the autumn countryside provides oodles atmosphere the falling leaves and low lying sun providing unsettling backdrop for the sinister events come the cast must said are all superb and are perfectly cast their respective roles the ide