1 |text this intensely involving 2007 character driven suspense drama like big juicy piece shakespearean level steak from master filmmaker who knows how draw out uncommonly ferocious the edge performances from his actors consider for starters henry fonda lone dissenting juror twelve angry men katharine hepburn delusional mary tyrone long day journey into night rod steiger conflicted concentration camp survivor the pawnbroker william holden wintry lion network and paul newman alcoholic lawyer the verdict the list encompasses some the finest screen work the past half century and you can safely add philip seymour hoffman desperately controlling andy hanson the ranks director sidney lumet shows signs octogenarian fatigue and fact revels the melodramatic turns first time screenwriter kelly masterson thickly plotted script the scale the story deceptively small focuses the moral compromises that unravel family where two brothers have become desperate for immediate cash woody allen followed similar fraternal dynamic his last film the oddly pinched cassandra dream but lumet neither pinched nor cautious his fierce approach this inescapable tale ambiguity and deception the plot revolves around crime that was meant victimless embezzling funds from his real estate company payroll keep his neglected wife gina happy and satisfy expensive drug habit smooth talking andy about exposed irs audit meanwhile his younger brother hank mass post divorce codependent insecurities falling way behind his alimony and child support payments andy concocts supposedly foolproof plan rob their parents suburban jewelry store while neither them supposed there the goal was for the brothers collect the haul and the parents claim the insurance murphy law intervenes every possible way starting with andy pressuring hank the job himself after some brotherly cajoling hank agrees but too scared alone recruits reckless gun toting busboy handle the robbery fate the heist occurs the one day that andy and hank mother opening the shop and things quickly spiral out control from there although the back and forth storytelling technique not new for example alejandro gonz xc3 xa1lez xc3 xb1 xc3 xa1rritu grams masterson approach works effectively delineating certain events from multiple perspectives that you understand how each character led the repercussions the unfortunate event the acting pitch perfect starting with hoffman riveting performance andy machiavellian reptile whose cool exterior and innate amorality mask layers resentment toward his family thought was great tamara jenkins the savages but even better here lumet even draws solid performance from the usually insufferable ethan hawke hank imbuing him with the emasculated weakness that informs his every ill planned move their embattled father albert finney acts with his typical late career bluster but provides the necessary foundation for the oedipal level complexities marisa tomei smart choice play gina the actress economically keys the responsive watchful nature small but pivotal role the estimable theater veteran rosemary harris now better known peter parker aunt the spider man trilogy has precious little time the mother does amy ryan hank bitter wife there are scenes that border excessive especially the situation becomes increasingly desperate for the brothers but the principals inject such energetic brio them that the flourishes become forgivable after the disappointment the cartoonish find guilty refreshing see lumet peak form here the 2008 dvd offers terrifically informative commentary from lumet hoffman and hawke all whom converse with ease and insight throughout along with the original theatrical trailer there also better than average minute featurette directed sidney lumet how the devil was made which features set footage and snippets interviews with lumet two the producers and the principal actors
