1 |text dramatic license some hate though necessary retelling any life story the case lucy the main points lucille ball teenage years early career and year marriage desi arnaz are all included albeit truncated and reworked way the main emotional points lucy life are made clear lucille struggle find her niche actress finally blossoming into the brilliant comedienne who made the character lucy ricardo legend her turbulent romantic and ultimately impossible marriage desi arnaz lucy desi creating the first television empire and forever securing their place history most memorable sitcom couple lucille ball rachel york does commendable job not expect see quite the same miraculous transformation like the one judy davis made when playing judy garland but york makes ball strong willed yet likable and very funny her own right even though her comedic timing different than lucy she still believable the film never goes into much detail about her perfectionistic behaviour the set and her mistreatment vivian vance during the early love lucy years but watching york portray lucy rehearsing privately nice inclusion daniel pino thinner and less charismatic than the real desi was but does have his own charm and does mostly decent job with desi accent especially the opening scene madeline zima was decent not overly memorable the teen aged lucy vivian vance and william frawley were not featured much thankfully since rebecca hobbs and russell newman were not very convincing the roles not that they aren good actors their own right they just were not all that suited the people they were playing most the actors were from austrailia and new zeland and the repressed accents are detectable times although the main structure the film sticks historical fact there are many deviations some for seemingly inexplicable reasons jess oppenheimer the head writer lucy radio show favourite husband which began 1948 depicted this film arriving the scene help with love lucy 1951 completely disregarding the fact that was the main creator this movie also depicts marc daniels being the main love lucy director for its entire run completely ignoring the fact that was replaced william asher after the first season also though figure this was due budgetary constraints the ricardo are shown live the same apartment for their entire stay new york when reality they changed apartments 1953 the kitchen set slightly larger and off scale from the original well the connecticut home looks pretty close the original except the right and left sides the house have been condensed and restructured there also desi talking about buying rko 1953 during lucy red scare incident even though rko did not hit the market until 1957 these changes well could have been for dramatic license and the film does work conveying the main facts but would have hurt them show bit more respect oppenheimer and asher two vital figures love lucy history the biggest gaff comes the love lucy recreation scenes least few them always risky recreating something that captured film and has been seen billions people but even more when obvious changes are made the scene with the giant bread loaf was truncated and anyone all familiar with that episode would have noticed the differences right away the having baby number was shortened well but other than that was practically dead far the best was the grape stomping scene with rachel york really nailing lucy mannerisms the producers made the wise decision not attempt directly recreating the vitametavegamin and candy factory bits instead showing the actors rehearse them these scenes proved effective because that approach the film main fault that makes the assumption the viewers already know great deal about lucy life since much skimmed over omitted all overall though gives decent portrait lucy desi marriage and the factual errors can overlooked when the character development works effectively
