1 |text decidedly not the target audience for this film man nearly who has only recently stumbled across the world independent film this happened quite accident with the discovery movie called clerks late one night television the first two things noticed about that film were that was technically amateurish and brilliantly written when read interview with the director the local paper and said that one his influences was clerks started get interesting when said his main influence was the station agent movie seen dvd week prior decided had and check out the result could described along the same lines clerks although the two films are nothing alike content wise both films suffer from technical gaffes that are overcome through amazing writing whereas clerks day the life man who has nothing his life all and afraid ask tough questions about himself and his situation less like about man who seemingly forces himself constantly busy always running one way another filling his life with little things that will never have deal with the big ones the themes and ideas this film are strong and poignant can tell from watching that not much has changed since was growing young men still have the same problems they always have the writer dresses these problems and themes the modern vernacular crafts wonderfully honest characters and has them completely believable things far indie cinema goes this may not perfect from technical standpoint but from artistic one very close
