1 |text comments for vivah its charming idealistic love story starring shahid kapoor and amrita rao the film takes back small pleasures like the bride and bridegroom families sleeping the floor playing games together their friendly banter and mutual respect vivah about the sanctity marriage and the importance commitment between two individuals yes the central romance naively visualized but the sneaked romantic moments between the married couple and their stubborn resistance modern courtship games makes you crave for the idealism the film predictably concludes with the marriage and the groom the wedding night tells his new bride who suffers from burn injuries come let your dressing showcases lot good things beauty arranged marriage beauty indian culture beauty indian woman last but not least nice idealism the about couple waiting get married playing the rules simple yet beautiful such simple story plot villain the case with most sooraj barjatya films sooraj sir back what does best has made the movie with full conviction its very sweet film which teaches the current generation lot good things bout arranged marriage the union families think amrita rao looks very good she has acted very well she has most the good scenes although thought the last half hour was completely shahid kapur who for change gives awesomely restrained performance also liked the acting all others for the choti amrita prakash alok nath anupam kher shahid bro sis law almost seemed real and recognizable could sooraj sir has got another nice family film his credit after maine pyar kiya hahk hum saath saath hain the chemistry between shahid amrita awesome stuff like sanctity marriage relationship avoiding courtship mutual respect care space waiting for getting married officially praying sacrficing for beloved all these and more get showcased vivah there still some good audience who going enjoying this film some the folks audience are already excited after seeing that they thinking bout arranged marriage thats success you ask seems amrita rao our actress from vivah result for nice performance has been bestowed the prestigious dadsaheb phalke award for 2006 hats off her for this achievement chalo even though vivah shahid amrita didn get any the film fare other awards least this news cheer about congrats amrita rao for showing visual indian bride the purest form and course sooraj barjatya for portraying her the best way shudn forget shahid kapur and all others who make vivah sweet and legendary today imagine share the same pedestal the legendary dilip kumar its mean achievement congrats amrita rao for taking her career another level with this award personally feel she should keep doing movies only with shahid kapur they make cute couple and their screen chemistry reminds srk kajol aamir khan juhi chawla some points that observed few the elements notice carefully amrita rao looks good because shes always wearing traditional dresses she gives every bit the indian woman essence this film perfect fit shahid kapur like most not exactly ready for marriage early marriage but prem listens carefully the step wise talk given his dad having full faith anupam kher eventually honesty trust are the keywords that reflects his first talk with amrita most people would think such first meeting with total stranger plus for limited time never enough judge person but according what saw this film have feeling that two people who are made for each other can connect within 1st meet also its possible the entire movie there are basically sequences where shahid amrita are together shown together its unlike most other romantic wedding based movies where hero heroine are always singing dancing nowadays doing cheap stuff but the beauty each these sequences characterized restraint innocence respect for the other really liked the relationship shown between chacha alok nath amrita rao these kinda movies should highlight the indifference shown daughters girl kids some parts india romantic scenes between lead couple are shot very nicely cheap scenes songs are beautifully pictured words like jal praarthana are going buzzwords for all girls who liked this film personally really fond many dialogs this film last but not the least the entire hospital scene where shahid puts sindhoor amrita when shes struggling for life terrific those dialogs between the couple are touching and feel the love cant without its hats off feeling many ways vivah reminded maine pyar kiya ddlj qayamat qayamat tak hum dil chuke sanam for the freshness screen chemistry the lead pair ask along with films like rang basanti lage raho munnabhai dor corporate and kabul express ranks among the best films made 2006 fact think vivah does deserve better viewing business than dhoom2 fanaa golmaal all those time pass fuzzy style crap movies
