1 |text first saw this film during and international film studies course non traditional student and perhaps for reasons years lived wisdom accrued appreciated the slow reflective pacing the film narrative languorous with the heat and dust arid clime the story deeply psychological replete with multi layered symbolism and articulate inversion the theme being the other land that one does not understand the understanding that does come fraught with the unresolved memories and subjectivity the outsider made nearly years ago also forerunner genre numerous other international films that explore the themes colonials colonized spaces clueless the nuances the cultures into which they have entered much more lavishly filmed and heavily financed works that have been made since reflect the same themes indochine nowhere africa are two that comparison perhaps make chocolat seem pale and boring has adrenaline pumping action extreme violence the struggles are mental emotional and subtle but that being said fine film worth viewing
