1 |text since the title english and imdb lists this show primary language english shall concentrate reviewing the english version gundam wing 2000 presented the bandai released dvd set actual review for the whole series under imdb entry shin kid xc3 xb4 senki gundam 1995 very little changed respect plot script and characterization its adaptation english and really depends your own taste choose which language watch this show purists can stick japanese all they want but for more realistic experience recommend the english track since all the characters except heero yuy are not japanese most them are caucasian fact with couple non japanese asians for one thing the characters personalities come across more directly than the japanese version the contrast between the characters stronger thanks some give take performances but very well cast group actors wing gundam pilot heero yuy highly trained soldier who suppresses his emotions but slowly learns the value his humanity voiced mark hildreth who deadpan delivery can criticized bad acting but matches heero personality very well deathscythe gundam duo maxwell ever cheerful the face death given crash course the cherishing the value life and friends possibly the best acted character the whole show masterfully played scott mcneil may sound little too old for his age but duo english voice easily out ranks his irritatingly nasal japanese one trowa the pilot heavyarms lost lonely soul who only purpose far has been combat despite his inner desire form connections with the people around him only knows how kill not befriend kirby morrow gives somber but realistic performance trowa barton quatre rebarba winner voiced brad swaile who has trouble brining out the caring nature the character and the shattering his innocence experiences horrors war and death first hand huge plus point that quatre longer sounds like girl and yes voiced female actress the japanese version but bona fide typical year old guy the impulsive but determined wufei chang voiced ted cole may seem little over the top but plays out stark contrast the more subdued roles heero and trowa relena darlian sounds older english voiced lisa ann bailey this might not sit well with her youthful personification early the series but her character matures later into the story her voice follows suit and ends fitting very well with the character development zechs merquise would one the more drastically changed voices when compared the japanese version both voices bring out different sides the same character his japanese voice haughty authoritative and commands respect keeping line with his high ranking status and charismatic nature his english voice brian drummond more subdued sounding more devious and snake like highlighting zechs secretive nature regarding his hidden agendas and staunch beliefs his ideals the members are mixed bag really treize kushrenada voiced david kaye given more realistic and down earth performance compared his larger than life japanese style speaking however lady une does not convey her split personality contrastingly the japanese version and lucrencia noin just sounds bored most the time the cannon fodder pilots and military leaders are nothing speak either would have appreciated they took the time give different characters different accents reflect their ethnic backgrounds the maganac corp voices were generally uninspired but could have been more interesting they were given middle eastern accents the members the romerfeller foundation would have also sounded better with some classy european accent that reflects their status nobility despite underwhelming acting from the side characters the main cast manage carry the show and results overall less over the top and more realistic rendition gundam wing script very faithful the original japanese script keeping all the underlying thought provoking ideas and themes about politics war and human nature sadly also retains the flaws the original japanese script
