1 |text the most succinct way describe ride with the devil with but one word authenticity will not rehash what has already been said about this wonderous film but would like say how much the historical research and painstaking attention detail the crew doubt went through was appreciated this filmgoer student history familiar with the period and setting this film must say that this production one the most accurate fictional films regarding bleeding kansas yes there were liberties taken the actual events all fiction apt but the overall feel the film genuine authentic costumes authentic attitudes hindsight here even the actors look authentic even jewel kilcher who has small part the film looked like she stepped form mid 19th century photograph few viewers talked with have expressed their incredulity the stylized dialog they cannot believe that 19th century farmers would talk like poets what they don realize that this age verbal slobbishness the american public public the 19th century was surprisingly literate and eloquent bunch these people were raised shakespeare and the king james version the bible the screenwriters reconstructed the most likely verbal styles these people judging from documentation the time the stylized dialog just adds the magical atmosphere the film but addition historical document this film works visceral level well beautifully photographed and performed harkens back the days the great western epics the raid lawrence kansas done many times before many other lesser films portrayed with sense urgency that puts the viewer right the midst the action romance adventure moral and ethical conflict this film has everything discerning moviegoer could want year that was dominated overhyped garbage like american beauty this great artwork was buried indifferent studio system but certain that ride with the devil will given due the coming years please rent this film you will not disappointed
