1 |text richard attenborough director whose name synonymous with the academy award winning gandhi back didn know any other work his till recently came across cry freedom released back 1987 while may not have been popular his gandhi every bit gripping not more and was released when south africa still had not got rid the shackles apartheid while most movies social issues come out after the event had happened guess this one released during the time the story based real life characters and events the book which the movie was based was written donald woods kevin kline journalist who used work south africa until the end the seventies traces the origins woods friendship with the charismatic black leader steve biko who wonderfully portrayed denzel washington cannot imagine better choice for the role washington exudes natural charm and screen presence which biko character required while initially woods was against what felt was black racism being spread biko after meeting the man could not help being drawn into his struggles and ideas the bond between them grows stronger and woods and his family realise and become more sensitive the plight the people biko represents however finally tragedy strikes and woods must now concentrate escaping from south africa with his book that can get published and let the outside world know what going the second half the movie gripping tale his escape from south africa along with his family and will keep you tenterhooks there are some deliciously humorous dialogues too the scene between biko and the lawyer the courtroom example lawyer you advocate violence biko advocate confrontation lawyer well isn that violence biko biko not necessarily you and are having confrontation now but don see any violence however there are moments that bring you back the horrors that pervaded the country before better sense prevailed the scene where the army opens fire protest school children gut wrenching and heartbreaking this definitely must watch would suggest those not familiar with attenborough work take time out for this there are movies which make lot money and there are movies which make lives would any day prefer the latter
