1 |text the legend andrei konchalovsky towering and half hour poem siberia not begin once because must hold back for space because takes its time roundabout explorations half remembered childhood memories turn the century backwoods village yet the movie goes picking steam building emotional resonance though even the sounds and images which compose become imbued sheer association with their subject matter with that quality fierce tireless quiet dignity that characterizes the soviet working spirit konchalovsky celebrates soviet collectivity but almost revisionist way paeans like soy cuba and invincible the mood turns somber and reflective news the revolution reach the secluded siberian village through the grapevine the fruits its labor reach only when world war calls for the young men enlist through all this konchalovksy zeroes the individual with care and affection examine the bitter longing and regret the woman who waited years after the war for fianc xc3 xa9 who never came back waited long enough out and become barmaid ship with velvet couches and which she quit years later come back her village care for aging uncle who killed the fianc xc3 xa9 father with axe the irreverent folly the fianc xc3 xa9 who came back from the war hero years too late came back not for the sake the girl left behind but drill oil for the motherland the despair and resignation the middle aged regional party leader who comes back his small siberian village with the sole purpose blotting out the map build power plant the movie segues from decade decade from the the with amazing newsreel footage trailing soviet history from the revolution war famine and the titanic technological achievements empire terrific visuals here all kinetic violence and skewed angles and flickering cramped shots crowds and faces but the actual movie focuses the individual triumphs and follies small and big the second half sense bittersweet fatalism creeps broken lives that never reached fulfillment choking with regret and yearning can matter seems like the world saying which konchalovksy answers must matter because the protagonists keep trying for redemption yet behind this saga man against landscape something seems hover shadowy almost substanceless like the eternal old man hermit who appears every segment guide repudiate the protagonists sometimes mere spectactor sometimes the enigmatic sage little behind and above all the other straightforward and logical incomprehensible ultimatums challenges and affirmations the human characters something invisible seems lurk ghosts the fathers appearing sepia dreams repeated shots star gleaming the nightsky curious bear indeed the eternal old man himself konchalovksy calls for awe and reverence before mystical land some other order its treatment small backwoods community struggling against nature progress and time and the ways learns deal with them often funny bizarre and tragic the same time and how the director never allows cynicism override his humanism reminds shohei imamura the profound desires the gods when dream scene alexei tears through the planks door which plastered propaganda poster stalin reach out his dead father vanishes the fog the movie hints the betrayal the soviet dream better yet all the things lost the revolution this betrayal made more explicit the film fiery denouement the amazing visuals elegiac and somber with raw naturalist edge help seal the deal the end oil derric erupts flames and the movie erupts wild explosion pure cinema
