1 |text deliverance brilliant condensed epic group thoroughly modern men who embark canoe trip briefly commune with nature and instead have fight for their sanity their lives and perhaps even their souls the film has aged well despite being made the early seventies certainly doesn look particularly dated still possesses visceral punch and iconic status dramatic post death the sixties philosophical and cultural shock vehicle there are very few films with similar conceits that can compare favourably although the legendary sam peckinpah stuff would have there yes there has been considerable debate and discussion about the film most confronting scene which won expand upon here and undoubtedly one the most confronting scenes the entire history the cinematic medium but what surprises about this film how achingly beautiful times this seems generally overlooked yet retrospect quite understandably the cinematography that captures the essence the vanishing fragile river wilderness often absolutely stunning and counterbalances the film moment brief madness the viewers along with the characters themselves are plunged into unrelenting nightmare deliverance narrative fittingly lean and sinewy and surprising how quickly events unfold from point establishment through crisis and aftermath all takes place very quickly which lends sense very real urgency the film the setting established effectively through the opening credits the characters are all well drawn despite limited time spent back story know just enough about them know them for the kind man they are like them and ultimately fear for them when all goes hell the conflict and violence within the movie seems erupt out nowhere with frightening lack logic this author james dickey theme that any prevailing romanticism about the nature man perceived inherent goodness can only wilt and die when his barely suppressed animal instincts come the fore there are demons bogeymen here the predatory hillbillies the film central villains are merely crude terrifyingly amoral cousins our protagonists they shock because their evil petty and tangible the film has peripheral characters all reflect something about the weaknesses and uncertainties urbanised homo sapiens the latter 20th century and all are very real and recognisable burt reynolds wonderful this movie the gung and almost fatally over confident survivalist lewis and shame think that really couldn recapture his brief moment dramatic glory throughout the rest his still sputtering and down career boogie nights excluded perhaps trust your are not reynolds fan you will impressed with his performance here john voight his usual effortlessly accomplished self and ned beatty and ronny cox both make significant contributions this simply great quartet actors conclude must speculate and when deliverance author james dickey the white sea will made for those that enjoyed this film ttws similarly harrowing tale american air force pilot struggle for survival after being shot down over the japanese mainland during ww2 more the typically bleak existentialism and primordial savagery that dickey trademark but has all the makings truly spectacular poetic cinematic experience there was the suggestion few years ago that the coen brothers might producing but that eventually came nothing being avid coen phile disappoints think what might have been had they gotten the green light ttws rather than their last couple relatively undistinguished efforts returning deliverance impossible imagine movie such honest unnerving brutality being made these times and that pretty shameful the cinema going public are all the poorer for this
