1 |text things come indeed classic work speculative fiction both essay the destructive nature war and the terrors progress makes some surprising accurate depictions the war that was follow few years later but woefully naive utopian ideals raymond massey cedric hardwicke and ralph richardson make fine cast although the drama played more stage piece than work cinema there are grandiose somewhat stilted speeches often delivered the actor trying reach the back the theater however there are some profound words there technology the savior mankind the instrument its destruction the film visual feast one can detach oneself from the age the effects sure hollywood more sophisticated today but rarely inventive for the imaginative the third act treat world with underground cities massive deco bombers space cannons gyro copters and secret organizations scientist saviors has all the makings sci pulp adventure but instead uses the trappings for philosophical exercise things come and metropolis were the hallmarks neolithic hollywood science fiction cinema they are operatic scope and visually inspiring technology has long left them behind but their ideas still burst forth there artistry there one with more heart and emotion than the computer generated mass produced cinema today these films are the products artisans not industrialists
