1 |text not easy film watch over three and half hours long and composed entirely conversations yet incredibly compelling and ruthlessly observational the human character that humble opinion one the very greatest films all time the film depressing cynical and cruel you want something uplifting see jacques rivette fantastic xc3 xa9line and julie boating which was made around the same time shows the idealism the late 1960s nothing different from the society that was trying change involves supposedly liberated xc3 xa9nage xc3 xa0 trois between alexandre played jean pierre leaud marie bernadette lafont and veronika francoise lebrun yet alexandre shown chauvinistic and jealous any other man the women are exposed being willingly subservient and defining their femininity through the male gaze the film extremely icy end the highly revolutionary french new wave this movement was one the most significant movements film history and had profound effect cinema know jean pierre leaud was one the key actors the new wave having starred among other films the influential les quatres cent coups 1959 francois truffaut rebellious teenager director jean eustache not well known other directors from the new wave but should there improvisation unlike john cassavetes similar films made the and the dialogue comes from real life conversations the film resonant with eustache personal experiences for example francoise lebrun was former lover eustache eustache himself committed suicide 1981 and the real life person that the character marie was based did too the anger and bitterness all culminate harrowing monologue veronika delivered directly the audience breaking down the coldly objective nature the rest the film this mesmerising personal and honest filmic statement remains one the most revealing films human nature around
