1 |text despite being quite far removed from expectations was thoroughly impressed dog bite dog rented not knowing much about but essentially expected martial arts action film the standard hong kong action tradition which devoted fan ended getting something entirely different which not all bad thing while the film could classified such and there definitely some good action and hand hand combat scenes the film definitely not the primary focus its characters are infinitely more important the film than its fights rather uncommon thing many hong kong action movies was really quite surprised the intricacy the characters and character relationships the film the lead character played edison chen who really very good becomes infinitely more complex the end the film than ever thought would after watching the first thirty minutes the police characters also defied expectations thoroughly fact the stark and honest portrayal the seldom seen dark side the police force was quite possible favorite aspect the film don know that would say dog bite dog entirely subverts typical notions bad criminal good cop but certainly distorts them ways not often seen film unfortunately many films especially hong kong action films find portray police what frankly very ignorantly idealized light this one least favorite things about the genre was pleasantly surprised see that dog bite dog actually had some very unique and really quite courageous ideas present about the police force there are negotiation scenes this film that have never seen the likes before and doubt will ever see again and sure will remember for quite while also the criminal characters are shown from interesting perspective well there some documentary footage the film cambodian boys older than ten being made fight each other the death with their bare hands which thought was one the film most powerful and moving moments says lot about the reason these guys are the way they are rather than simply condemning them also the relationship between chen character and the girl meets the junk yard reveals lot about his character wasn until this element entered the film that really started see the film emotional experience rather than only visceral one there something about most screen relationships that doesn quite get through but for some reason this one really did the actress does incredible job with this role which imagine was not easy play dog bite dog also features some really breathtaking cinematography all though unfortunately rather uneven there were some moments that found really striking particularly the last segment the film but there was also good deal camera work that was just another slight problem had was with the pacing which also felt was uneven found lot the looking for boat scenes little alienating all though quickly picks after that the action scenes are short and not too plentiful but are truly powerful and effecting particularly towards the end the fight choreography honestly not all that impressive for the most part all though its credit solid and fairly realistic but the true strength the emotional content behind the fights the final scene while not marvel martial artistry fight choreography one the most powerful final fights have ever seen and seen quite few martial arts films suppose the biggest determining factor whether not one will get much out dog bite dog whether not you can connect with the characters all them are certainly some the more flawed characters one likely see film any kind but there was something very human about all them that couldn help but drawn and really feel for them particularly chen girlfriend should say that doubt most people will like the film much did simply because imagine that most people will not like care about the characters the same way but still recommend highly all the same truly deeply moving and effecting film you give chance
