1 |text need recap the plot since others have done already understandable that many viewers find fault with the film raised are with the slam bang sensurround today cineplex experience against that background movie like ecstasy appears have wandered from another planet think there are several worthwhile reasons why most importantly the film unfolds poetically the camera pans slowly over surrounding hills trees clouds etc providing serene and lyrical sense natural world that integrates the man and woman into its fold together these reveal style and dimension almost totally missing from today technology driven cinema where rapid fire editing works divert audience attention and not concentrate additionally the story conveyed eye and not ear with almost dialogue explain what happening this amounts another extreme departure from today very literal fare where visuals only seem count when they excite the audience but perhaps most unsettling the movie sometimes eerily quiet not the sense that silent films are quiet since expect them but the sense that the characters seldom speak when expect them thus the burden the story shared between the film maker and the viewer the former must choose his visuals artfully convey the narrative while the latter must think about those visuals since they not going explained none this intended belittle today film making simply point out that movie like machaty comes out very different aesthetic from the one have today don claim either any better worse however claim that ecstasy represents perspective sorely missing from today movie going experience where such contemplative values are routinely dismissed slow and boring the film itself masterpiece though times reaches artistic heights the beautifully composed beer garden scene with its final crane shot rising reveal the exquisite tableau below the slow pans the countryside with its pantheistic celebration life nature and regeneration are also wonderfully expressed these are the kind scenes that don overwhelm you but instead given half chance accumulate quietly into experience memorable its own way the spine tingling variety jaws the other hand the film sometimes heavy handed when machaty piles the imagery particularly the final ode labor sequence hard know what make this rather disruptive presence perhaps the symbolism has with the heroic dimension that hard work holds for the love lorn hero and people general theme then being promoted the influential soviet cinema still its presence here rather tediously over done anyhow got admit that tuned initially see the gorgeous hedy lamarr the buff but now have admit that the process also got lot more than just peek boo romp the woods
