1 |text the film design seems the alpha and omega some the major issues this country see relationships all over the university setting for the film befittingly the obvious student teacher present but what the film adds its value its other relationships male female white black and the individual society but most important all and direct relation all the other relationships the individual himself was amazed how bilateral point view the director gave showing the race relations campus most films typically show the injustices one side while showing the suffering the other this film showed the injustices and suffering both sides did not attempt show how either was right although would say the skin heads were shown much crueler and vindictive quite obvious towards the end the film also discusses sex and rape ironically this injustice that some ways brings the two races together for time lawrence fishburne does over the top performance the sagacious profesor phipps crumbles the idea race favortism and instead shows the parallelism the lazy and down trodden with the industrious and positive other stars that make this film are omar epps ice cube and jennifer connelly michael rapaport gives excellent portrayal confused youth with misplaced anger who looking for acceptance tyra banks make her film debut and proves supermodels can act higher learning gets its name showing college more than going class and getting piece paper fact would say the film almost satire showing students interactions with each other rather than some dry book the real education university life learning process not textual one think you find higher learning apropos the important issues many universities and even life general
