1 |text fantastic show and unrealized classic the league gentlemen remains one the greatest modern comedies recent times with dark and bizarre style humor that towers over the tired formulaic approach inferior yet unfortunately far more acknowledged successor little britain the league gentlemen was truly something special during rather quiet era british comedy until arrival the scene there had never really been anything like the league gentlemen before the surface seemingly simplistic sketch show the show soon unfolds vivid sinister but incredibly hilarious universe populated with all manner brilliant comedic creations what really sets the show apart from rivals approach telling story rather than serve hashed sketches barely distinguishable from the next here see each individual group characters through their various journeys and story lines visit them the same and each time they offer with surprise gradually over three series and christmas special the fictional town royston vasey heaving with grotesque yet hilarious populace and that probably the main reason why the show such joy watch and also the reason why the show would easily merit more series unlike other current shows like the catherine tate show more importantly little britain the league both know when character has run course and have the opportunity deal with that several fan favorite who could have easily been kept entertain further bowed out before the series came close giving room for fellow characters grow more allow for the introduction newer residents royston vasey make their mark another thing that sets this show above others that the writing team approach the script process with care and intelligence mentioned before all four members the league have sound mind when comes judging the longevity their creations and when time call quits respect certain characters this awareness has also meant the league gentlemen undergoes bold evolution not usually seen show this nature the narrative driven and far darker third series brave step away from the more sketch based first two series and this bold move the league really pays off with the third series there less urgency for them please audience and like the christmas special they pursue individual stories with clear narrative unlike the more sketch based previous series that succesfully binded together various sets sketches into series long story arc the third series both refreshing change pace style well real treat for fans who already seen the first two despite some polarized opinion the third series any real fan the league will appreciate what the third series has offer well really enjoy the more character based episodes that only delve deeper into fan favorite but pair and inter wine characters that might not have crossed paths previously might take little trying get into the change style but definitely worth and opinion the third series the best and also provides firm conclusion the series the show not without drawbacks and very occasionally certain characters and set pieces appear somewhat out place but for the most part the genius writing dark nature the show and the host brilliant characters that are often all too close real life make for real treat and prove what comedy should about and puts much the more recent catch phrase driven and often desperate attempts comedy shame
