1 |text august 1980 the disappearance baby azaria chamberlain and the pursuant trial her parents lindy and michael for the alleged murder the child caused uproar across what was then very angry nation the media and the public had already tried and convicted the accused couple and were baying for blood what followed was gross miscarriage justice michael and lindy chamberlain claimed that while camping near ayers rock central australia that dingo had taken their ten week old daughter from their tent they were preparing eat the barbecue area one believed them lindy was charged with the murder her baby and michael accessory after the fact the whole country was abuzz with whispers ritual killing the chamberlain trial was over before began lindy never proved her innocence she was found guilty there was never enough evidence convict her yet the jury was swayed public and media pressure how could nation even sit judgement from where are how could possibly presume know unless there was absolute proof and reasonable doubt whatsoever the chamberlains should have been acquitted fred schepisi film unequivocally and whole heartedly supports the argument john bryson novel that the chamberlains were completely innocent the charges laid against them that fact dingo did take baby azaria that fateful night ayers rock schepisi has brilliantly captured the mood blood thirsty nation hell bent the truth being brought light shows australia rather unbecoming light people who were totally obsessed with seeing the chamberlains pay his screenplay written with robert caswell vigorously stirs the emotions and will most certainly find the audience saddened and angered the travesty justice which occurred the outstanding meryl streep gives incredible performance the woman accused the most dreadful acts she brings life most convincingly the tough little aussie who was ready stand the allegations and set the world straight even her accent almost but not quite spot very good effort the master that trade sam neill every bit good streep the first faithful but then disillusioned michael who cannot comprehend why their world falling apart and starts question his christianity his was streep showing great emotional strength that will move you profoundly the entire support cast are also excellent with some australia finest actors and actresses playing part technically the film brilliant too with director photography ian baker capturing this great land with splendour especially the rock editor jill bilcock keeps the whole movie tense and very emotionally charged while bruce smeaton provides telling score for all aussies this must see shocking look the mirror you will what country did family who just wanted justice served and the truth known michael chamberlain said don think anybody really understands what innocence means innocent people saturday may 1995 video even return viewings fred schepisi account the travesty justice that befell the chamberlains who lost baby azaria ayres rock 1980 still emotionally powerful and honestly moving schepisi and robert caswell have expertly transferred john bryson novel the screen telling with simplicity the horrifying story vacation gone terribly wrong for michael and lindy chamberlain whose new born daughter azaria was taken form the family tent dingo just moments after being put down amid media speculation and vicious public rumour lindy was charged with the murder her baby and michael was charged accessory after the fact what followed was little more than trial media and with the australian people determined she put away lindy was found guilty and sentenced life imprisonment with hard labour even though the prosecution could present motive and little other than circumstantial evidence meryl streep top form the accused woman who battles australia head prove her innocence she truly awesome and the only thing that fails her true blue aussie accent though she does her level best sound ocker you might wonder why top australian actress wasn cast the role but star power probably the answer alongside meryl equally impressive sam neill outstanding the husband who sees his world falling apart before his eyes while feels powerless anything about strong aussie cast lend compelling support editing from jill bilcock very timely ian baker cinematography the rock and other rugged locations visually brilliant and bruce smeaton music perfect for the part truly must for all conscientious australians sunday june 1996 video
