1 |text walt disney his old men put their own 1950 spin the classic fairy tale cinderella which guess you could say helps form unofficial fairy tale princess trilogy from the classic disney years the plot cinderella nice girl who can catch break she the daughter nice wealthy widower who loved her dearly but her mother passed away when cinderella was very young and cindy father felt she needed mother figure eventually married the woman who would become known lady tremaine herself widow with two daughters about the same age cinderella anastasia and drizella first they all seemed get along but then cinderella father died and lady tremaine true nature was revealed she was cold cruel callous heartless mean spirited woman and she passed those traits her daughters who were spoiled bratty and equally mean spirited anastasia drizella hate cinderella because they know deep down that she better looking and overall nicer more attractive lady than themselves more appealing men and their mother lady tremaine hates cindy for pretty much the same reasons the years passed lady tremaine began squander the family fortunes stubborn but futile quest improve refine her awkward unattractive daughters call them homely would insult homely people everywhere while all three relegated cinderella being the multi tasking servant the house abusing her mistreating her and humiliating her every chance they get they are particularly fond increasing her already absurd workload that brings cinderella the present where she has blossomed into good looking young lady who somehow manages remain kind hearted and nice despite her abusive step family and holds the hope that one day the tables will turn her favor cinderella gets her shot freedom happiness when royal ball held introduce the local prince eligible young maiden that can take her wife settle down start family etc naturally her step family tries keep her from attending even going far physically assault her and rip the dress she had procured for herself with little help from her mice friends the dress belonged her biological mother finally pushed beyond her breaking point cinderella runs out into the courtyard and cries despair that point that her fairy godmother short plump jolly woman arrives and provides cinderella with transportation and transformed dress after all cinderella wouldn make very good impression the ball she entered the scene looking like she had just gotten gang raped cindy arrives the ball the prince falls hard for her but that pesky midnight rule gets the way forcing her flee but leaving behind glass slipper make long story short after long harrowing quest find the mystery girl via trying the glass slipper cinderella found and she and the prince get married giving her the happy ending she deserves overall enjoyable disney classic not without its flaws the most glaring which that the prince little more than macguffin help push the plot along has very little screen time and even less dialogue never get know him very well get good look his relationship with cinderella which unfortunate since according the making documentary the prince was originally meant play bigger role and few additional scenes help flesh out cinderella herself might have been helpful there was song that showed her fantasizing turning into army maids clean the house well eavesdropping her step family post ball show her amusement their jealousy which was cut because walt himself thought made her look spiteful still cinderella herself likable enough heroine even she upstaged her mice friends and there sweetness the film that becoming harder find these days course this were being made now cinderella would probably put more struggle against her family during the dress ripping scene and would probably free herself the climax either picking the lock herself making impractical yet exciting jump down from her window but this beside the point and for all those who say cinderella sets bad example for young girls well consider this least cinderella didn around getting publicly drunk and indecently exposed unlike some modern day princesses you know who mean
